window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b093-99b9f09c2abd0903.json"]={sha256:"99b9f09c2abd0903543fadc2b79dfa052a180d88e6ff380342e7b7326d9b83e6",value:{"id":"b093","title":"鋼構耐火被覆施工","titleEn":"Structural-steel fireproofing application","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從鋼材在火害中的強度折減與臨界溫度出發，建立斷面係數與被覆厚度的熱傳關係，比較噴覆型防火材料（SFRM）與膨脹型防火塗料的材料機制、施工環境與交叉作業損傷，再以 ASTM E605／E736 現場抽驗、耐火試驗登錄與約束條件判讀完成驗收，並以世界貿易中心、紐約時報大樓與馬德里溫莎大樓說明厚度、黏結與改修過渡期的風險。","summaryEn":"Starting from steel strength loss and critical temperature in fire, build the heat-transfer link between section factor and protection thickness, compare the mechanisms, site conditions and trade damage of sprayed fire-resistive materials (SFRM) and intumescent coatings, then close acceptance with ASTM E605/E736 field sampling, fire-test listings and restraint classification, using the World Trade Center, the New York Times Building and the Windsor Building in Madrid to show the risks of thin spots, weak bond and half-finished retrofits.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-seismic-precast-fire","subcategoryTitle":"建築耐震、預鑄與防火","subcategoryTitleEn":"Building seismic, precast and fire safety","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-seismic-precast-fire","learningTags":["structures","st-seismic-precast-fire","fire"],"architectureFamily":"fire","architectureNodes":[["火災曝露與臨界溫度","Fire exposure and critical temperature"],["鋼構斷面係數","Steel section factor"],["噴覆或膨脹型被覆","Sprayed or intumescent protection"],["表面準備與施工順序","Surface preparation and sequencing"],["厚度密度黏結抽驗","Thickness, density and bond sampling"],["維護改修與交接紀錄","Maintenance, retrofit and handover records"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[3,2],[2,4],[4,5],[0,5]],"diagram":{"type":"fire","labels":["火災曝露與臨界溫度","鋼構斷面係數","噴覆或膨脹型被覆","表面準備與施工順序","厚度密度黏結抽驗"],"labelsEn":["Fire exposure and critical temperature","Steel section factor","Sprayed or intumescent protection","Surface preparation and sequencing","Thickness, density and bond sampling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：某 150 m（約 492 ft）辦公塔的樓板梁要求 2 小時非約束等級，選用的登錄設計以 W/D = 0.82 的試驗梁、SFRM 厚度 1.00 in 取得該等級。專案梁 W16×26：D = 3bf + 2d − 2tw = 3×5.50 + 2×15.7 − 2×0.25 = 47.4 in，W/D = 26/47.4 ≈ 0.55，換算斷面係數 Ap/V ≈ 134/(W/D) ≈ 244 m⁻¹；厚度 T₁ = 1.00×(0.82 + 0.6)/(0.55 + 0.6) = 1.42/1.15 ≈ 1.24 in，取 1.25 in（約 32 mm）。現場允收：設計 ≥ 1 in，單點不得低於 1.25 − 0.25 = 1.00 in。樓高超過 420 ft，黏結門檻 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa，以 0.0045 m² 拉拔蓋需承受約 215 N 不破壞。若改用 W16×40（D = 3×7.00 + 2×16.0 − 2×0.305 ≈ 52.4 in，W/D ≈ 0.76），T₁ = 1.42/1.36 ≈ 1.04 in，較重斷面可減薄約 0.2 in，但仍不得低於登錄最小厚度。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: floor beams in a 150 m (about 492 ft) office tower need a 2-hour unrestrained rating, and the chosen listed design achieved it with a test beam of W/D = 0.82 and 1.00 in of SFRM. Project beam W16×26: D = 3bf + 2d − 2tw = 3×5.50 + 2×15.7 − 2×0.25 = 47.4 in, W/D = 26/47.4 ≈ 0.55, equivalent to a section factor Ap/V ≈ 134/(W/D) ≈ 244 m⁻¹; thickness T₁ = 1.00×(0.82 + 0.6)/(0.55 + 0.6) = 1.42/1.15 ≈ 1.24 in, specified as 1.25 in (about 32 mm). Field acceptance: with a design of 1 in or more, no reading may be below 1.25 − 0.25 = 1.00 in. The tower exceeds 420 ft, so the bond threshold is 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa, meaning a 0.0045 m² pull-off cap must hold about 215 N. If a W16×40 is used instead (D = 3×7.00 + 2×16.0 − 2×0.305 ≈ 52.4 in, W/D ≈ 0.76), T₁ = 1.42/1.36 ≈ 1.04 in, so the heavier section saves about 0.2 in but must still respect the listed minimum. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b093-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「火害曝露與鋼材強度折減」與「斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fire exposure and steel strength loss\" and \"Section factor and heating of protected steel\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b093-v13-01","title":"火害曝露與鋼材強度折減：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fire exposure and steel strength loss: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「鋼構件臨界溫度」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Critical steel temperature” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"結構鋼在約 400°C 以上開始明顯損失降伏強度與彈性模數，600°C 左右只剩常溫強度的一半左右，而一般建築火災的煙層溫度在數十分鐘內即可超過 800°C。耐火被覆本身不承載，它的任務是延緩熱量進入鋼材，使構件在要求的耐火時效內仍低於「臨界溫度」，也就是剩餘強度恰好等於火災時載重效應的溫度。臨界溫度不是固定值：火災載重組合採用較低的活載重，構件利用率越低，可容許的溫度越高；梁柱的支承與約束條件也會改變破壞模式。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼構件臨界溫度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Structural steel begins to lose yield strength and stiffness noticeably above about 400°C and keeps only about half its ambient strength near 600°C, while gas temperatures in an ordinary building fire can exceed 800°C within tens of minutes. Fireproofing carries no load; its task is to slow heat flow into the steel so that, for the required fire-resistance period, the member stays below its critical temperature, the temperature at which the remaining strength just equals the load effect in fire. That temperature is not fixed: fire load combinations use reduced live load, a lower utilisation allows a higher temperature, and support and restraint conditions change the failure mode. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Critical steel temperature” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: EN 1993-1-2 gives the critical temperature θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼構件臨界溫度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Critical steel temperature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-01-k1","title":"火害曝露與鋼材強度折減","titleEn":"Fire exposure and steel strength loss","text":"結構鋼在約 400°C 以上開始明顯損失降伏強度與彈性模數，600°C 左右只剩常溫強度的一半左右，而一般建築火災的煙層溫度在數十分鐘內即可超過 800°C。耐火被覆本身不承載，它的任務是延緩熱量進入鋼材，使構件在要求的耐火時效內仍低於「臨界溫度」，也就是剩餘強度恰好等於火災時載重效應的溫度。","textEn":"Structural steel begins to lose yield strength and stiffness noticeably above about 400°C and keeps only about half its ambient strength near 600°C, while gas temperatures in an ordinary building fire can exceed 800°C within tens of minutes. Fireproofing carries no load; its task is to slow heat flow into the steel so that, for the required fire-resistance period, the member stays below its critical temperature, the temperature at which the remaining strength just equals the load effect in fire.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「火害曝露與鋼材強度折減」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fire exposure and steel strength loss\" is correct?","options":["鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。","結構鋼在約 400°C 以上開始明顯損失降伏強度與彈性模數，600°C 左右只剩常溫強度的一半左右，而一般建築火災的煙層溫度在數十分鐘內即可超過 800°C。","被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame.","Structural steel begins to lose yield strength and stiffness noticeably above about 400°C and keeps only about half its ambient strength near 600°C, while gas temperatures in an ordinary building fire can exceed 800°C within tens of minutes.","Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"結構鋼在約 400°C 以上開始明顯損失降伏強度與彈性模數，600°C 左右只剩常溫強度的一半左右，而一般建築火災的煙層溫度在數十分鐘內即可超過 800°C。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Structural steel begins to lose yield strength and stiffness noticeably above about 400°C and keeps only about half its ambient strength near 600°C, while gas temperatures in an ordinary building fire can exceed 800°C within tens of minutes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b093-v13-02","title":"火害曝露與鋼材強度折減：定量估算","titleEn":"Fire exposure and steel strength loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼構件臨界溫度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Critical steel temperature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。利用率 μ₀ = 0.6 時 θ_cr ≈ 554°C；μ₀ = 0.4 時 θ_cr ≈ 620°C。ISO 834 標準升溫 θ_g = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20 在 t = 60 min 時約 945°C，遠高於兩者，因此必須靠被覆延緩升溫。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: EN 1993-1-2 gives the critical temperature θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482. A utilisation μ₀ = 0.6 gives θ_cr ≈ 554°C; μ₀ = 0.4 gives θ_cr ≈ 620°C. The ISO 834 standard curve θ_g = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20 reaches about 945°C at t = 60 min, far above both, so protection must delay the heating. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在結構計算書列出每一類構件在火災載重組合下的利用率並換算臨界溫度，再對照所選耐火試驗登錄的允收溫度（ASTM E119 梁為四點平均 593°C、任一點 704°C）是否一致或較保守；若採性能化設計，需由防火工程師提出升溫分析，並經審查單位與主管建築機關認可。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List each member type's utilisation under the fire load combination in the structural calculations, convert it to a critical temperature, and check that the acceptance temperature of the chosen fire-test listing (ASTM E119 beams: 593°C average over four points, 704°C at any point) is consistent or more conservative; a performance-based design needs a heat-transfer analysis by a fire engineer, accepted by the peer reviewer and the building authority.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。利用率 μ₀ = 0.6 時 θ_cr ≈ 554°C；μ₀ = 0.4 時 θ_cr ≈ 620°C。ISO 834 標準升溫 θ_g = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20 在 t = 60 min 時約 945°C，遠高於兩者，因此必須靠被覆延緩升溫。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"EN 1993-1-2 gives the critical temperature θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482. A utilisation μ₀ = 0.6 gives θ_cr ≈ 554°C; μ₀ = 0.4 gives θ_cr ≈ 620°C. The ISO 834 standard curve θ_g = 345·log₁₀(8t+1) + 20 reaches about 945°C at t = 60 min, far above both, so protection must delay the heating. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「火害曝露與鋼材強度折減」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fire exposure and steel strength loss\", which statement holds?","options":["膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。","被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。","EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。"],"optionsEn":["As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating.","Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.","EN 1993-1-2 gives the critical temperature θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482."],"answer":2,"explanation":"EN 1993-1-2 臨界溫度 θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"EN 1993-1-2 gives the critical temperature θ_cr = 39.19·ln[1/(0.9674·μ₀^3.833) − 1] + 482. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b093-v13-03","title":"火害曝露與鋼材強度折減：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fire exposure and steel strength loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼構件臨界溫度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Critical steel temperature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在結構計算書列出每一類構件在火災載重組合下的利用率並換算臨界溫度，再對照所選耐火試驗登錄的允收溫度（ASTM E119 梁為四點平均 593°C、任一點 704°C）是否一致或較保守；若採性能化設計，需由防火工程師提出升溫分析，並經審查單位與主管建築機關認可。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List each member type's utilisation under the fire load combination in the structural calculations, convert it to a critical temperature, and check that the acceptance temperature of the chosen fire-test listing (ASTM E119 beams: 593°C average over four points, 704°C at any point) is consistent or more conservative; a performance-based design needs a heat-transfer analysis by a fire engineer, accepted by the peer reviewer and the building authority. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計圖應以表格列出每種構件的耐火時效、所依據的試驗登錄編號、利用率假設與所需厚度，並註明「變更斷面或載重須重新核算被覆」；這張表是監造、被覆廠商與檢驗員共同的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Drawings should tabulate for each member type the fire-resistance rating, the listing number relied on, the assumed utilisation and the required thickness, with a note that any change of section or load requires the fireproofing to be re-checked; this table is the common reference for the supervising engineer, applicator and inspector.","failure":"注意干擾：把所有構件一律套用相同被覆厚度而不看利用率與斷面，常造成重載的細長柱保護不足、輕載大梁卻過度保護；火災中保護不足的柱先達臨界溫度並縮短，迫使上方樓層荷重重分配，嚴重時引發連鎖破壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying one thickness to every member regardless of utilisation and section often leaves heavily loaded slender columns under-protected and lightly loaded girders over-protected; in a fire the under-protected column reaches its critical temperature first and shortens, forcing load redistribution in the floors above and, at worst, progressive failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在結構計算書列出每一類構件在火災載重組合下的利用率並換算臨界溫度，再對照所選耐火試驗登錄的允收溫度（ASTM E119 梁為四點平均 593°C、任一點 704°C）是否一致或較保守；若採性能化設計，需由防火工程師提出升溫分析，並經審查單位與主管建築機關認可。","textEn":"List each member type's utilisation under the fire load combination in the structural calculations, convert it to a critical temperature, and check that the acceptance temperature of the chosen fire-test listing (ASTM E119 beams: 593°C average over four points, 704°C at any point) is consistent or more conservative; a performance-based design needs a heat-transfer analysis by a fire engineer, accepted by the peer reviewer and the building authority.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計圖應以表格列出每種構件的耐火時效、所依據的試驗登錄編號、利用率假設與所需厚度，並註明「變更斷面或載重須重新核算被覆」；這張表是監造、被覆廠商與檢驗員共同的依據。","textEn":"Drawings should tabulate for each member type the fire-resistance rating, the listing number relied on, the assumed utilisation and the required thickness, with a note that any change of section or load requires the fireproofing to be re-checked; this table is the common reference for the supervising engineer, applicator and inspector.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「火害曝露與鋼材強度折減」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fire exposure and steel strength loss\"?","options":["在結構計算書列出每一類構件在火災載重組合下的利用率並換算臨界溫度，再對照所選耐火試驗登錄的允收溫度（ASTM E119 梁為四點平均 593°C、任一點 704°C）是否一致或較保守。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。"],"optionsEn":["List each member type's utilisation under the fire load combination in the structural calculations, convert it to a critical temperature, and check that the acceptance temperature of the chosen fire-test listing (ASTM E119 beams: 593°C average over four points, 704°C at any point) is consistent or more conservative.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在結構計算書列出每一類構件在火災載重組合下的利用率並換算臨界溫度，再對照所選耐火試驗登錄的允收溫度（ASTM E119 梁為四點平均 593°C、任一點 704°C）是否一致或較保守；若採性能化設計，需由防火工程師提出升溫分析，並經審查單位與主管建築機關認可。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List each member type's utilisation under the fire load combination in the structural calculations, convert it to a critical temperature, and check that the acceptance temperature of the chosen fire-test listing (ASTM E119 beams: 593°C average over four points, 704°C at any point) is consistent or more conservative; a performance-based design needs a heat-transfer analysis by a fire engineer, accepted by the peer reviewer and the building authority. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b093-v13-04","title":"火害曝露與鋼材強度折減：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fire exposure and steel strength loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼構件臨界溫度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Critical steel temperature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把所有構件一律套用相同被覆厚度而不看利用率與斷面，常造成重載的細長柱保護不足、輕載大梁卻過度保護；火災中保護不足的柱先達臨界溫度並縮短，迫使上方樓層荷重重分配，嚴重時引發連鎖破壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying one thickness to every member regardless of utilisation and section often leaves heavily loaded slender columns under-protected and lightly loaded girders over-protected; in a fire the under-protected column reaches its critical temperature first and shortens, forcing load redistribution in the floors above and, at worst, progressive failure. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：臨界溫度不是固定值：火災載重組合採用較低的活載重，構件利用率越低，可容許的溫度越高；梁柱的支承與約束條件也會改變破壞模式。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That temperature is not fixed: fire load combinations use reduced live load, a lower utilisation allows a higher temperature, and support and restraint conditions change the failure mode.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把所有構件一律套用相同被覆厚度而不看利用率與斷面，常造成重載的細長柱保護不足、輕載大梁卻過度保護；火災中保護不足的柱先達臨界溫度並縮短，迫使上方樓層荷重重分配，嚴重時引發連鎖破壞。","textEn":"Applying one thickness to every member regardless of utilisation and section often leaves heavily loaded slender columns under-protected and lightly loaded girders over-protected; in a fire the under-protected column reaches its critical temperature first and shortens, forcing load redistribution in the floors above and, at worst, progressive failure.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「火害曝露與鋼材強度折減」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fire exposure and steel strength loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把所有構件一律套用相同被覆厚度而不看利用率與斷面，常造成重載的細長柱保護不足、輕載大梁卻過度保護。","被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Applying one thickness to every member regardless of utilisation and section often leaves heavily loaded slender columns under-protected and lightly loaded girders over-protected.","Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把所有構件一律套用相同被覆厚度而不看利用率與斷面，常造成重載的細長柱保護不足、輕載大梁卻過度保護；火災中保護不足的柱先達臨界溫度並縮短，迫使上方樓層荷重重分配，嚴重時引發連鎖破壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying one thickness to every member regardless of utilisation and section often leaves heavily loaded slender columns under-protected and lightly loaded girders over-protected; in a fire the under-protected column reaches its critical temperature first and shortens, forcing load redistribution in the floors above and, at worst, progressive failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b093-v13-05","title":"斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Section factor and heating of protected steel: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「斷面係數 Ap/V」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Section factor Ap/V” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"受火鋼材的升溫速度取決於吸熱表面積與可儲熱鋼材體積之比，也就是斷面係數 Ap/V（美制以每呎重量與受熱周長之比 W/D 表示，意義相反）。同樣的被覆厚度包在薄腹細長斷面上升溫較快，包在厚重斷面上升溫較慢。被覆以低熱傳導係數形成熱阻，熱流大約與厚度成反比；含水的水泥系材料在約 100°C 時還會因水分蒸發出現升溫平台。三面受火（上方為樓板）與四面受火的周長不同，必須依實際構造計算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「斷面係數 Ap/V」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The heating rate of protected steel depends on the ratio of heated surface to the steel volume that stores heat, the section factor Ap/V (US practice uses weight per foot over heated perimeter, W/D, the inverse sense). The same protection thickness lets a thin-walled slender section heat faster than a heavy one. The protection forms a thermal resistance with low conductivity, so heat flow is roughly inversely proportional to thickness; moisture in cementitious products also produces a temperature plateau near 100°C as water evaporates. Three-sided exposure under a slab and four-sided exposure give different perimeters and must follow the actual construction. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Section factor Ap/V” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：輕質被覆的集總升溫率 Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For light protection the lumped heating rate is Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa).","failure":"常見誤解：「被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「斷面係數 Ap/V」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Section factor Ap/V”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-05-k1","title":"斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫","titleEn":"Section factor and heating of protected steel","text":"受火鋼材的升溫速度取決於吸熱表面積與可儲熱鋼材體積之比，也就是斷面係數 Ap/V（美制以每呎重量與受熱周長之比 W/D 表示，意義相反）。同樣的被覆厚度包在薄腹細長斷面上升溫較快，包在厚重斷面上升溫較慢。","textEn":"The heating rate of protected steel depends on the ratio of heated surface to the steel volume that stores heat, the section factor Ap/V (US practice uses weight per foot over heated perimeter, W/D, the inverse sense). The same protection thickness lets a thin-walled slender section heat faster than a heavy one.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Section factor and heating of protected steel\" is correct?","options":["被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。","噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。","受火鋼材的升溫速度取決於吸熱表面積與可儲熱鋼材體積之比，也就是斷面係數 Ap/V（美制以每呎重量與受熱周長之比 W/D 表示，意義相反）。"],"optionsEn":["Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section.","Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.","The heating rate of protected steel depends on the ratio of heated surface to the steel volume that stores heat, the section factor Ap/V (US practice uses weight per foot over heated perimeter, W/D, the inverse sense)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"受火鋼材的升溫速度取決於吸熱表面積與可儲熱鋼材體積之比，也就是斷面係數 Ap/V（美制以每呎重量與受熱周長之比 W/D 表示，意義相反）。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The heating rate of protected steel depends on the ratio of heated surface to the steel volume that stores heat, the section factor Ap/V (US practice uses weight per foot over heated perimeter, W/D, the inverse sense). The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b093-v13-06","title":"斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫：定量估算","titleEn":"Section factor and heating of protected steel: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷面係數 Ap/V」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Section factor Ap/V” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：輕質被覆的集總升溫率 Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa)。取 λp = 0.12 W/m·K、dp = 25 mm、Ap/V = 150 m⁻¹、θg − θa = 800 K、ca = 600 J/kg·K、ρa = 7,850 kg/m³：(0.12/0.025)×150×800×60 s/(600×7,850) ≈ 7.3 K/min；厚度加倍為 50 mm 時約 3.7 K/min。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For light protection the lumped heating rate is Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa). With λp = 0.12 W/m·K, dp = 25 mm, Ap/V = 150 m⁻¹, θg − θa = 800 K, ca = 600 J/kg·K and ρa = 7,850 kg/m³: (0.12/0.025)×150×800×60 s/(600×7,850) ≈ 7.3 K/min; doubling the thickness to 50 mm gives about 3.7 K/min. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：從鋼構深化圖取出每一斷面尺寸，依三面或四面受火計算受熱周長與斷面係數，與廠商厚度表或試驗登錄的適用範圍比對；超出範圍（斷面係數過大或過小）時不可外插，須取得廠商或試驗機構出具的工程判定書。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Take each section's dimensions from the steel shop drawings, compute heated perimeter and section factor for three- or four-sided exposure, and compare with the range of the manufacturer's thickness tables or the test listing; outside that range, with a section factor too high or too low, do not extrapolate but obtain an engineering judgement from the manufacturer or test body.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"輕質被覆的集總升溫率 Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa)。取 λp = 0.12 W/m·K、dp = 25 mm、Ap/V = 150 m⁻¹、θg − θa = 800 K、ca = 600 J/kg·K、ρa = 7,850 kg/m³：(0.12/0.025)×150×800×60 s/(600×7,850) ≈ 7.3 K/min；厚度加倍為 50 mm 時約 3.7 K/min。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For light protection the lumped heating rate is Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa). With λp = 0.12 W/m·K, dp = 25 mm, Ap/V = 150 m⁻¹, θg − θa = 800 K, ca = 600 J/kg·K and ρa = 7,850 kg/m³: (0.12/0.025)×150×800×60 s/(600×7,850) ≈ 7.3 K/min; doubling the thickness to 50 mm gives about 3.7 K/min. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Section factor and heating of protected steel\", which statement holds?","options":["輕質被覆的集總升溫率 Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa)。","只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。","平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。"],"optionsEn":["For light protection the lumped heating rate is Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa).","If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection.","If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"輕質被覆的集總升溫率 Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For light protection the lumped heating rate is Δθ/Δt ≈ (λp/dp)·(Ap/V)·(θg − θa)/(ca·ρa). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b093-v13-07","title":"斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Section factor and heating of protected steel: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷面係數 Ap/V」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Section factor Ap/V” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"從鋼構深化圖取出每一斷面尺寸，依三面或四面受火計算受熱周長與斷面係數，與廠商厚度表或試驗登錄的適用範圍比對；超出範圍（斷面係數過大或過小）時不可外插，須取得廠商或試驗機構出具的工程判定書。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Take each section's dimensions from the steel shop drawings, compute heated perimeter and section factor for three- or four-sided exposure, and compare with the range of the manufacturer's thickness tables or the test listing; outside that range, with a section factor too high or too low, do not extrapolate but obtain an engineering judgement from the manufacturer or test body. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：深化圖階段由鋼構廠輸出每支構件的斷面係數清單，被覆廠商據此提出逐件厚度表並簽章；現場每支構件以噴漆或標籤標示所需厚度，讓施作人員與檢驗員不必在現場自行換算。","observationEn":"Site practice: At shop-drawing stage the steel fabricator issues a section-factor list for every member, the fireproofing contractor returns a signed member-by-member thickness schedule, and each member on site is marked with its required thickness so that applicators and inspectors never recalculate in the field.","failure":"注意干擾：把四面受火周長套用到頂部有樓板的梁，或把箱形柱當成 H 型鋼計算，斷面係數算錯會直接造成厚度不足或浪費；另一常見錯誤是忽略蜂巢梁與腹板開孔梁的薄腹板，局部升溫遠快於翼板。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a four-sided perimeter for a beam under a slab, or treating a box column as an H-section, gives a wrong section factor and directly produces too little or wasted thickness; another common error ignores the thin webs of cellular or castellated beams, which heat much faster locally than the flanges. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"從鋼構深化圖取出每一斷面尺寸，依三面或四面受火計算受熱周長與斷面係數，與廠商厚度表或試驗登錄的適用範圍比對；超出範圍（斷面係數過大或過小）時不可外插，須取得廠商或試驗機構出具的工程判定書。","textEn":"Take each section's dimensions from the steel shop drawings, compute heated perimeter and section factor for three- or four-sided exposure, and compare with the range of the manufacturer's thickness tables or the test listing; outside that range, with a section factor too high or too low, do not extrapolate but obtain an engineering judgement from the manufacturer or test body.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"深化圖階段由鋼構廠輸出每支構件的斷面係數清單，被覆廠商據此提出逐件厚度表並簽章；現場每支構件以噴漆或標籤標示所需厚度，讓施作人員與檢驗員不必在現場自行換算。","textEn":"At shop-drawing stage the steel fabricator issues a section-factor list for every member, the fireproofing contractor returns a signed member-by-member thickness schedule, and each member on site is marked with its required thickness so that applicators and inspectors never recalculate in the field.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Section factor and heating of protected steel\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","從鋼構深化圖取出每一斷面尺寸，依三面或四面受火計算受熱周長與斷面係數，與廠商厚度表或試驗登錄的適用範圍比對。","防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Take each section's dimensions from the steel shop drawings, compute heated perimeter and section factor for three- or four-sided exposure, and compare with the range of the manufacturer's thickness tables or the test listing.","Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"從鋼構深化圖取出每一斷面尺寸，依三面或四面受火計算受熱周長與斷面係數，與廠商厚度表或試驗登錄的適用範圍比對；超出範圍（斷面係數過大或過小）時不可外插，須取得廠商或試驗機構出具的工程判定書。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Take each section's dimensions from the steel shop drawings, compute heated perimeter and section factor for three- or four-sided exposure, and compare with the range of the manufacturer's thickness tables or the test listing; outside that range, with a section factor too high or too low, do not extrapolate but obtain an engineering judgement from the manufacturer or test body. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b093-v13-08","title":"斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫：失效診斷","titleEn":"Section factor and heating of protected steel: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷面係數 Ap/V」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Section factor Ap/V” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把四面受火周長套用到頂部有樓板的梁，或把箱形柱當成 H 型鋼計算，斷面係數算錯會直接造成厚度不足或浪費；另一常見錯誤是忽略蜂巢梁與腹板開孔梁的薄腹板，局部升溫遠快於翼板。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a four-sided perimeter for a beam under a slab, or treating a box column as an H-section, gives a wrong section factor and directly produces too little or wasted thickness; another common error ignores the thin webs of cellular or castellated beams, which heat much faster locally than the flanges. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：三面受火（上方為樓板）與四面受火的周長不同，必須依實際構造計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Three-sided exposure under a slab and four-sided exposure give different perimeters and must follow the actual construction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把四面受火周長套用到頂部有樓板的梁，或把箱形柱當成 H 型鋼計算，斷面係數算錯會直接造成厚度不足或浪費；另一常見錯誤是忽略蜂巢梁與腹板開孔梁的薄腹板，局部升溫遠快於翼板。","textEn":"Using a four-sided perimeter for a beam under a slab, or treating a box column as an H-section, gives a wrong section factor and directly produces too little or wasted thickness; another common error ignores the thin webs of cellular or castellated beams, which heat much faster locally than the flanges.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「斷面係數與受保護鋼材升溫」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Section factor and heating of protected steel\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。","把四面受火周長套用到頂部有樓板的梁，或把箱形柱當成 H 型鋼計算，斷面係數算錯會直接造成厚度不足或浪費。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.","Using a four-sided perimeter for a beam under a slab, or treating a box column as an H-section, gives a wrong section factor and directly produces too little or wasted thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把四面受火周長套用到頂部有樓板的梁，或把箱形柱當成 H 型鋼計算，斷面係數算錯會直接造成厚度不足或浪費；另一常見錯誤是忽略蜂巢梁與腹板開孔梁的薄腹板，局部升溫遠快於翼板。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a four-sided perimeter for a beam under a slab, or treating a box column as an H-section, gives a wrong section factor and directly produces too little or wasted thickness; another common error ignores the thin webs of cellular or castellated beams, which heat much faster locally than the flanges. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b093-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「噴覆材料密度與厚度換算」與「膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"SFRM density and thickness substitution\" and \"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b093-v13-09","title":"噴覆材料密度與厚度換算：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"SFRM density and thickness substitution: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「噴覆型防火材料 SFRM」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sprayed fire-resistive material” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"SFRM 以石膏或水泥為膠結材，加入礦物纖維、蛭石或輕質骨材，濕噴或乾噴於鋼材表面，固化後形成多孔隔熱層。標準密度產品（約 15–21 pcf，240–336 kg/m³）適用於隱蔽空間；中、高密度產品抗衝擊與黏結較佳，用於停車場、機房或外露區。耐火試驗只對特定試體斷面取得厚度，其他斷面須以經認可的換算式調整：較重的斷面（W/D 較大）吸熱能力較高，可用較薄的被覆，但不得低於登錄的最小厚度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「噴覆型防火材料 SFRM」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"SFRM uses a gypsum or cement binder with mineral fibre, vermiculite or lightweight aggregate, sprayed wet or dry onto the steel and cured into a porous insulating layer. Standard-density products (about 15–21 pcf, 240–336 kg/m³) suit concealed spaces; medium- and high-density products resist impact and bond better and are used in car parks, plant rooms or exposed areas. A fire test establishes thickness only for the tested section, so other sections are adjusted with an accepted substitution equation: heavier sections with higher W/D absorb more heat and may take a thinner coat, but never below the listed minimum thickness. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Sprayed fire-resistive material” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：梁斷面替代式 T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Beam substitution T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6).","failure":"常見誤解：「噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「噴覆型防火材料 SFRM」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Sprayed fire-resistive material”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-09-k1","title":"噴覆材料密度與厚度換算","titleEn":"SFRM density and thickness substitution","text":"SFRM 以石膏或水泥為膠結材，加入礦物纖維、蛭石或輕質骨材，濕噴或乾噴於鋼材表面，固化後形成多孔隔熱層。標準密度產品（約 15–21 pcf，240–336 kg/m³）適用於隱蔽空間；中、高密度產品抗衝擊與黏結較佳，用於停車場、機房或外露區。","textEn":"SFRM uses a gypsum or cement binder with mineral fibre, vermiculite or lightweight aggregate, sprayed wet or dry onto the steel and cured into a porous insulating layer. Standard-density products (about 15–21 pcf, 240–336 kg/m³) suit concealed spaces; medium- and high-density products resist impact and bond better and are used in car parks, plant rooms or exposed areas.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「噴覆材料密度與厚度換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"SFRM density and thickness substitution\" is correct?","options":["SFRM 以石膏或水泥為膠結材，加入礦物纖維、蛭石或輕質骨材，濕噴或乾噴於鋼材表面，固化後形成多孔隔熱層。","噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。","膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。"],"optionsEn":["SFRM uses a gypsum or cement binder with mineral fibre, vermiculite or lightweight aggregate, sprayed wet or dry onto the steel and cured into a porous insulating layer.","Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.","As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"SFRM 以石膏或水泥為膠結材，加入礦物纖維、蛭石或輕質骨材，濕噴或乾噴於鋼材表面，固化後形成多孔隔熱層。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"SFRM uses a gypsum or cement binder with mineral fibre, vermiculite or lightweight aggregate, sprayed wet or dry onto the steel and cured into a porous insulating layer. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b093-v13-10","title":"噴覆材料密度與厚度換算：定量估算","titleEn":"SFRM density and thickness substitution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「噴覆型防火材料 SFRM」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sprayed fire-resistive material” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：梁斷面替代式 T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6)。W16×26 三面受火周長 D = 3bf + 2d − 2tw = 3×5.50 + 2×15.7 − 2×0.25 = 47.4 in，W/D = 26/47.4 ≈ 0.55。若試驗梁 W/D = 0.82、厚度 1.00 in，則 T₁ = 1.00×1.42/1.15 ≈ 1.24 in，取 1.25 in（約 32 mm）。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Beam substitution T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6). A W16×26 with three-sided exposure has D = 3bf + 2d − 2tw = 3×5.50 + 2×15.7 − 2×0.25 = 47.4 in, so W/D = 26/47.4 ≈ 0.55. If the tested beam has W/D = 0.82 and 1.00 in of protection, T₁ = 1.00×1.42/1.15 ≈ 1.24 in, specified as 1.25 in (about 32 mm). Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：確認所選登錄設計允許使用替代式、替代式只用於以溫度判定的非約束梁等級、計算結果不低於 3/8 in 等最小厚度，並把每一斷面的換算過程附在送審文件；同時核對產品密度等級與使用環境（隱蔽、外露、潮濕）相符。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm that the chosen listed design permits substitution, that the equation is applied only to the temperature-based unrestrained beam rating, and that results respect minimum thicknesses such as 3/8 in; attach the calculation for each section to the submittal, and check that the product density class matches the exposure: concealed, exposed or damp.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"梁斷面替代式 T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6)。W16×26 三面受火周長 D = 3bf + 2d − 2tw = 3×5.50 + 2×15.7 − 2×0.25 = 47.4 in，W/D = 26/47.4 ≈ 0.55。若試驗梁 W/D = 0.82、厚度 1.00 in，則 T₁ = 1.00×1.42/1.15 ≈ 1.24 in，取 1.25 in（約 32 mm）。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Beam substitution T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6). A W16×26 with three-sided exposure has D = 3bf + 2d − 2tw = 3×5.50 + 2×15.7 − 2×0.25 = 47.4 in, so W/D = 26/47.4 ≈ 0.55. If the tested beam has W/D = 0.82 and 1.00 in of protection, T₁ = 1.00×1.42/1.15 ≈ 1.24 in, specified as 1.25 in (about 32 mm). Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「噴覆材料密度與厚度換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"SFRM density and thickness substitution\", which statement holds?","options":["被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。","梁斷面替代式 T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6)。","約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。"],"optionsEn":["Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.","Beam substitution T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6).","A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used."],"answer":1,"explanation":"梁斷面替代式 T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Beam substitution T₁ = T₂·(W₂/D₂ + 0.6)/(W₁/D₁ + 0.6). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b093-v13-11","title":"噴覆材料密度與厚度換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"SFRM density and thickness substitution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「噴覆型防火材料 SFRM」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sprayed fire-resistive material” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"確認所選登錄設計允許使用替代式、替代式只用於以溫度判定的非約束梁等級、計算結果不低於 3/8 in 等最小厚度，並把每一斷面的換算過程附在送審文件；同時核對產品密度等級與使用環境（隱蔽、外露、潮濕）相符。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm that the chosen listed design permits substitution, that the equation is applied only to the temperature-based unrestrained beam rating, and that results respect minimum thicknesses such as 3/8 in; attach the calculation for each section to the submittal, and check that the product density class matches the exposure: concealed, exposed or damp. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規範應依區域指定密度等級（外露區與停車場用中、高密度），並要求廠商提交產品登錄、替代計算與現場密度試驗計畫；任何以較薄厚度取代設計值的提案，都須經結構與防火設計者書面同意。","observationEn":"Site practice: The specification should assign density classes by zone, with medium or high density for exposed areas and car parks, and require listings, substitution calculations and a field density-testing plan; any proposal to use a thinner coat than designed needs written approval from the structural and fire designers.","failure":"注意干擾：把梁的替代式用在柱，或為較輕斷面減少厚度，等於拿試驗沒有涵蓋的條件冒險；把標準密度產品噴在經常受碰撞的停車場或機房，短期內就被撞落、刮除，留下大片裸露鋼材。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using the beam equation for columns, or reducing thickness for a lighter section, gambles on conditions the test never covered; spraying standard-density product in a car park or plant room that sees frequent impact soon leaves it knocked off and scraped away, exposing large areas of bare steel. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"確認所選登錄設計允許使用替代式、替代式只用於以溫度判定的非約束梁等級、計算結果不低於 3/8 in 等最小厚度，並把每一斷面的換算過程附在送審文件；同時核對產品密度等級與使用環境（隱蔽、外露、潮濕）相符。","textEn":"Confirm that the chosen listed design permits substitution, that the equation is applied only to the temperature-based unrestrained beam rating, and that results respect minimum thicknesses such as 3/8 in; attach the calculation for each section to the submittal, and check that the product density class matches the exposure: concealed, exposed or damp.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規範應依區域指定密度等級（外露區與停車場用中、高密度），並要求廠商提交產品登錄、替代計算與現場密度試驗計畫；任何以較薄厚度取代設計值的提案，都須經結構與防火設計者書面同意。","textEn":"The specification should assign density classes by zone, with medium or high density for exposed areas and car parks, and require listings, substitution calculations and a field density-testing plan; any proposal to use a thinner coat than designed needs written approval from the structural and fire designers.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「噴覆材料密度與厚度換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"SFRM density and thickness substitution\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。","確認所選登錄設計允許使用替代式、替代式只用於以溫度判定的非約束梁等級、計算結果不低於 3/8 in 等最小厚度，並把每一斷面的換算過程附在送審文件。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating.","Confirm that the chosen listed design permits substitution, that the equation is applied only to the temperature-based unrestrained beam rating, and that results respect minimum thicknesses such as 3/8 in."],"answer":2,"explanation":"確認所選登錄設計允許使用替代式、替代式只用於以溫度判定的非約束梁等級、計算結果不低於 3/8 in 等最小厚度，並把每一斷面的換算過程附在送審文件；同時核對產品密度等級與使用環境（隱蔽、外露、潮濕）相符。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm that the chosen listed design permits substitution, that the equation is applied only to the temperature-based unrestrained beam rating, and that results respect minimum thicknesses such as 3/8 in; attach the calculation for each section to the submittal, and check that the product density class matches the exposure: concealed, exposed or damp. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b093-v13-12","title":"噴覆材料密度與厚度換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"SFRM density and thickness substitution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「噴覆型防火材料 SFRM」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sprayed fire-resistive material” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把梁的替代式用在柱，或為較輕斷面減少厚度，等於拿試驗沒有涵蓋的條件冒險；把標準密度產品噴在經常受碰撞的停車場或機房，短期內就被撞落、刮除，留下大片裸露鋼材。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using the beam equation for columns, or reducing thickness for a lighter section, gambles on conditions the test never covered; spraying standard-density product in a car park or plant room that sees frequent impact soon leaves it knocked off and scraped away, exposing large areas of bare steel. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：耐火試驗只對特定試體斷面取得厚度，其他斷面須以經認可的換算式調整：較重的斷面（W/D 較大）吸熱能力較高，可用較薄的被覆，但不得低於登錄的最小厚度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fire test establishes thickness only for the tested section, so other sections are adjusted with an accepted substitution equation: heavier sections with higher W/D absorb more heat and may take a thinner coat, but never below the listed minimum thickness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把梁的替代式用在柱，或為較輕斷面減少厚度，等於拿試驗沒有涵蓋的條件冒險；把標準密度產品噴在經常受碰撞的停車場或機房，短期內就被撞落、刮除，留下大片裸露鋼材。","textEn":"Using the beam equation for columns, or reducing thickness for a lighter section, gambles on conditions the test never covered; spraying standard-density product in a car park or plant room that sees frequent impact soon leaves it knocked off and scraped away, exposing large areas of bare steel.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「噴覆材料密度與厚度換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"SFRM density and thickness substitution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把梁的替代式用在柱，或為較輕斷面減少厚度，等於拿試驗沒有涵蓋的條件冒險；把標準密度產品噴在經常受碰撞的停車場或機房，短期內就被撞落、刮除，留下大片裸露鋼材。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。"],"optionsEn":["Using the beam equation for columns, or reducing thickness for a lighter section, gambles on conditions the test never covered.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把梁的替代式用在柱，或為較輕斷面減少厚度，等於拿試驗沒有涵蓋的條件冒險；把標準密度產品噴在經常受碰撞的停車場或機房，短期內就被撞落、刮除，留下大片裸露鋼材。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using the beam equation for columns, or reducing thickness for a lighter section, gambles on conditions the test never covered; spraying standard-density product in a car park or plant room that sees frequent impact soon leaves it knocked off and scraped away, exposing large areas of bare steel. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b093-v13-13","title":"膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「膨脹型防火塗料」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Intumescent coating” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"膨脹型防火塗料在常溫下只是一層數百微米到數毫米的塗膜，受熱到約 200–250°C 時，酸源、碳源與發泡劑反應，膨脹成多孔炭化層；薄塗型膨脹比可達約 50 倍，厚塗環氧型膨脹較小但耐候與抗衝擊較佳，常用於建築師希望保留鋼構外形的外露梁柱。塗膜是一個系統：底漆提供防蝕與附著，膨脹層提供耐火，面漆提供耐候與顏色；三者必須在試驗中一起驗證，任意更換底漆或面漆都可能讓炭化層剝落或膨脹不足。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「膨脹型防火塗料」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An intumescent coating is only a film of a few hundred microns to a few millimetres at ambient temperature; at about 200–250°C its acid source, carbon source and blowing agent react and swell into a porous char. Thin-film products can expand about 50 times, while thick-film epoxy types expand less but resist weather and impact better; they are used where architects want exposed beams and columns to keep their steel profile. The film is a system: the primer gives corrosion protection and adhesion, the intumescent layer gives fire resistance and the topcoat gives weathering and colour. All three must be proven together in testing, and swapping a primer or topcoat can make the char detach or under-expand. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Intumescent coating” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：乾膜厚 DFT = 濕膜厚 WFT × 體積固含量 VS。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Dry film thickness DFT = wet film thickness WFT × volume solids VS.","failure":"常見誤解：「膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「膨脹型防火塗料」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Intumescent coating”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-13-k1","title":"膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容","titleEn":"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility","text":"膨脹型防火塗料在常溫下只是一層數百微米到數毫米的塗膜，受熱到約 200–250°C 時，酸源、碳源與發泡劑反應，膨脹成多孔炭化層；薄塗型膨脹比可達約 50 倍，厚塗環氧型膨脹較小但耐候與抗衝擊較佳，常用於建築師希望保留鋼構外形的外露梁柱。塗膜是一個系統：底漆提供防蝕與附著，膨脹層提供耐火，面漆提供耐候與顏色；三者必須在試驗中一起驗證，任意更換底漆或面漆都可能讓炭化層剝落或膨脹不足。","textEn":"An intumescent coating is only a film of a few hundred microns to a few millimetres at ambient temperature; at about 200–250°C its acid source, carbon source and blowing agent react and swell into a porous char. Thin-film products can expand about 50 times, while thick-film epoxy types expand less but resist weather and impact better; they are used where architects want exposed beams and columns to keep their steel profile.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility\" is correct?","options":["膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。","膨脹型防火塗料在常溫下只是一層數百微米到數毫米的塗膜，受熱到約 200–250°C 時，酸源、碳源與發泡劑反應，膨脹成多孔炭化層。","只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。"],"optionsEn":["As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating.","An intumescent coating is only a film of a few hundred microns to a few millimetres at ambient temperature.","If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"膨脹型防火塗料在常溫下只是一層數百微米到數毫米的塗膜，受熱到約 200–250°C 時，酸源、碳源與發泡劑反應，膨脹成多孔炭化層；薄塗型膨脹比可達約 50 倍，厚塗環氧型膨脹較小但耐候與抗衝擊較佳，常用於建築師希望保留鋼構外形的外露梁柱。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An intumescent coating is only a film of a few hundred microns to a few millimetres at ambient temperature; at about 200–250°C its acid source, carbon source and blowing agent react and swell into a porous char. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b093-v13-14","title":"膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容：定量估算","titleEn":"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「膨脹型防火塗料」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Intumescent coating” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：乾膜厚 DFT = 濕膜厚 WFT × 體積固含量 VS。目標 DFT 2.10 mm、VS = 70%、每道最大 WFT 1.0 mm，則每道 DFT = 0.70 mm，需 3 道；理論用量 2.10/0.70 = 3.0 L/m²，計入 30% 損耗為 3.0/0.7 ≈ 4.3 L/m²。若膨脹 50 倍，1.0 mm 薄塗膜約形成 50 mm 炭化層。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Dry film thickness DFT = wet film thickness WFT × volume solids VS. For a target DFT of 2.10 mm, VS = 70% and a maximum WFT of 1.0 mm per coat, each coat gives 0.70 mm DFT, so 3 coats are needed; theoretical consumption is 2.10/0.70 = 3.0 L/m², or 3.0/0.7 ≈ 4.3 L/m² with 30% loss. At 50-fold expansion a 1.0 mm thin film forms about 50 mm of char. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對塗裝系統（底漆、膨脹層、面漆）與評估報告或試驗登錄（如 EN 13381-8 或 UL 設計）所列產品完全一致；施工中以濕膜梳量測每道濕膜，乾燥後以磁感式膜厚計依斷面分區量測乾膜，平均值須達要求、最低讀值在允許範圍內，並扣除底漆與面漆厚度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check that the system of primer, intumescent and topcoat matches exactly the products in the assessment report or listing, for example EN 13381-8 or a UL design; during work measure each wet coat with a comb gauge, and after drying measure DFT with a magnetic gauge zone by zone on each section, requiring the mean to reach the target and the lowest readings to stay within tolerance, after deducting primer and topcoat thickness.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"乾膜厚 DFT = 濕膜厚 WFT × 體積固含量 VS。目標 DFT 2.10 mm、VS = 70%、每道最大 WFT 1.0 mm，則每道 DFT = 0.70 mm，需 3 道；理論用量 2.10/0.70 = 3.0 L/m²，計入 30% 損耗為 3.0/0.7 ≈ 4.3 L/m²。若膨脹 50 倍，1.0 mm 薄塗膜約形成 50 mm 炭化層。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Dry film thickness DFT = wet film thickness WFT × volume solids VS. For a target DFT of 2.10 mm, VS = 70% and a maximum WFT of 1.0 mm per coat, each coat gives 0.70 mm DFT, so 3 coats are needed; theoretical consumption is 2.10/0.70 = 3.0 L/m², or 3.0/0.7 ≈ 4.3 L/m² with 30% loss. At 50-fold expansion a 1.0 mm thin film forms about 50 mm of char. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。","防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。","乾膜厚 DFT = 濕膜厚 WFT × 體積固含量 VS。"],"optionsEn":["If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected.","Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.","Dry film thickness DFT = wet film thickness WFT × volume solids VS."],"answer":2,"explanation":"乾膜厚 DFT = 濕膜厚 WFT × 體積固含量 VS。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Dry film thickness DFT = wet film thickness WFT × volume solids VS. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b093-v13-15","title":"膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「膨脹型防火塗料」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Intumescent coating” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對塗裝系統（底漆、膨脹層、面漆）與評估報告或試驗登錄（如 EN 13381-8 或 UL 設計）所列產品完全一致；施工中以濕膜梳量測每道濕膜，乾燥後以磁感式膜厚計依斷面分區量測乾膜，平均值須達要求、最低讀值在允許範圍內，並扣除底漆與面漆厚度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check that the system of primer, intumescent and topcoat matches exactly the products in the assessment report or listing, for example EN 13381-8 or a UL design; during work measure each wet coat with a comb gauge, and after drying measure DFT with a magnetic gauge zone by zone on each section, requiring the mean to reach the target and the lowest readings to stay within tolerance, after deducting primer and topcoat thickness. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：工廠塗裝與現場塗裝要劃清界面：哪些構件在廠內完成、運輸吊裝損傷由誰修補、接合部位留白多少與如何補塗，都要寫入塗裝計畫；底漆或面漆變更須取得塗料廠商的相容性書面確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw a clear line between shop and site application: which members are finished in the shop, who repairs transport and erection damage, how much is left bare at connections and how it is made good must all be in the coating plan; any primer or topcoat change needs the coating manufacturer's written compatibility confirmation.","failure":"注意干擾：面漆過厚或使用未經驗證的面漆會壓住膨脹，火災時炭化層只有設計的一部分；底漆不相容則可能讓整片塗膜受熱脫落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An over-thick or unproven topcoat can restrain expansion so the char reaches only part of its design thickness; an incompatible primer may let the whole film fall away when heated. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對塗裝系統（底漆、膨脹層、面漆）與評估報告或試驗登錄（如 EN 13381-8 或 UL 設計）所列產品完全一致；施工中以濕膜梳量測每道濕膜，乾燥後以磁感式膜厚計依斷面分區量測乾膜，平均值須達要求、最低讀值在允許範圍內，並扣除底漆與面漆厚度。","textEn":"Check that the system of primer, intumescent and topcoat matches exactly the products in the assessment report or listing, for example EN 13381-8 or a UL design; during work measure each wet coat with a comb gauge, and after drying measure DFT with a magnetic gauge zone by zone on each section, requiring the mean to reach the target and the lowest readings to stay within tolerance, after deducting primer and topcoat thickness.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"工廠塗裝與現場塗裝要劃清界面：哪些構件在廠內完成、運輸吊裝損傷由誰修補、接合部位留白多少與如何補塗，都要寫入塗裝計畫；底漆或面漆變更須取得塗料廠商的相容性書面確認。","textEn":"Draw a clear line between shop and site application: which members are finished in the shop, who repairs transport and erection damage, how much is left bare at connections and how it is made good must all be in the coating plan; any primer or topcoat change needs the coating manufacturer's written compatibility confirmation.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility\"?","options":["核對塗裝系統（底漆、膨脹層、面漆）與評估報告或試驗登錄（如 EN 13381-8 或 UL 設計）所列產品完全一致。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。"],"optionsEn":["Check that the system of primer, intumescent and topcoat matches exactly the products in the assessment report or listing, for example EN 13381-8 or a UL design.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對塗裝系統（底漆、膨脹層、面漆）與評估報告或試驗登錄（如 EN 13381-8 或 UL 設計）所列產品完全一致；施工中以濕膜梳量測每道濕膜，乾燥後以磁感式膜厚計依斷面分區量測乾膜，平均值須達要求、最低讀值在允許範圍內，並扣除底漆與面漆厚度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check that the system of primer, intumescent and topcoat matches exactly the products in the assessment report or listing, for example EN 13381-8 or a UL design; during work measure each wet coat with a comb gauge, and after drying measure DFT with a magnetic gauge zone by zone on each section, requiring the mean to reach the target and the lowest readings to stay within tolerance, after deducting primer and topcoat thickness. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b093-v13-16","title":"膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「膨脹型防火塗料」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Intumescent coating” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"面漆過厚或使用未經驗證的面漆會壓住膨脹，火災時炭化層只有設計的一部分；底漆不相容則可能讓整片塗膜受熱脫落。單道塗得過厚還會流垂、溶劑封在膜內而起泡，乾膜讀值看似足夠，內部卻有空洞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An over-thick or unproven topcoat can restrain expansion so the char reaches only part of its design thickness; an incompatible primer may let the whole film fall away when heated. A single coat applied too thick sags or traps solvent and blisters, so the DFT reading looks adequate while the film contains voids. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：塗膜是一個系統：底漆提供防蝕與附著，膨脹層提供耐火，面漆提供耐候與顏色；三者必須在試驗中一起驗證，任意更換底漆或面漆都可能讓炭化層剝落或膨脹不足。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: All three must be proven together in testing, and swapping a primer or topcoat can make the char detach or under-expand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"面漆過厚或使用未經驗證的面漆會壓住膨脹，火災時炭化層只有設計的一部分；底漆不相容則可能讓整片塗膜受熱脫落。單道塗得過厚還會流垂、溶劑封在膜內而起泡，乾膜讀值看似足夠，內部卻有空洞。","textEn":"An over-thick or unproven topcoat can restrain expansion so the char reaches only part of its design thickness; an incompatible primer may let the whole film fall away when heated. A single coat applied too thick sags or traps solvent and blisters, so the DFT reading looks adequate while the film contains voids.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膨脹型塗料與塗裝系統相容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Intumescent coatings and coating-system compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","面漆過厚或使用未經驗證的面漆會壓住膨脹，火災時炭化層只有設計的一部分；底漆不相容則可能讓整片塗膜受熱脫落。","只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An over-thick or unproven topcoat can restrain expansion so the char reaches only part of its design thickness.","If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面漆過厚或使用未經驗證的面漆會壓住膨脹，火災時炭化層只有設計的一部分；底漆不相容則可能讓整片塗膜受熱脫落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An over-thick or unproven topcoat can restrain expansion so the char reaches only part of its design thickness; an incompatible primer may let the whole film fall away when heated. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b093-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「表面準備、環境條件與施工順序」與「交叉作業損傷與等效厚度」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing\" and \"Trade damage and equivalent thickness\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b093-v13-17","title":"表面準備、環境條件與施工順序：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「鋼材表面與環境條件」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Substrate and ambient conditions” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"被覆能否在火災時留在鋼材上，首先取決於施工當天的表面與環境：油汙、軋鋼鱗片、浮鏽或不相容的底漆會降低黏結，結露的鋼面會讓塗膜附著不良，低溫則使水泥系材料無法正常水化。SFRM 通常在樓板混凝土澆置、鋼承板與吊架夾具完成後施作，以免後續焊接或鑽孔破壞被覆；但若太晚，管線與風管已擋住鋼梁，噴槍無法到達。施工順序因此是品質的一部分，而不只是進度問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼材表面與環境條件」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Whether protection stays on the steel in a fire depends first on the surface and ambient conditions on the day of application: oil, mill scale, loose rust or an incompatible primer reduce bond, condensation on the steel prevents coating adhesion, and low temperature stops cementitious products from hydrating properly. SFRM is normally applied after the slab is cast and deck attachments and hanger clips are installed, so that later welding or drilling does not damage it; but if it comes too late, pipes and ducts already shield the beams and the spray gun cannot reach. Sequencing is therefore part of quality, not just of programme. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Substrate and ambient conditions” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Magnus 露點 Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ)，γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Magnus dew point Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ), with γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T).","failure":"常見誤解：「只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼材表面與環境條件」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Substrate and ambient conditions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-17-k1","title":"表面準備、環境條件與施工順序","titleEn":"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing","text":"被覆能否在火災時留在鋼材上，首先取決於施工當天的表面與環境：油汙、軋鋼鱗片、浮鏽或不相容的底漆會降低黏結，結露的鋼面會讓塗膜附著不良，低溫則使水泥系材料無法正常水化。SFRM 通常在樓板混凝土澆置、鋼承板與吊架夾具完成後施作，以免後續焊接或鑽孔破壞被覆；但若太晚，管線與風管已擋住鋼梁，噴槍無法到達。","textEn":"Whether protection stays on the steel in a fire depends first on the surface and ambient conditions on the day of application: oil, mill scale, loose rust or an incompatible primer reduce bond, condensation on the steel prevents coating adhesion, and low temperature stops cementitious products from hydrating properly. SFRM is normally applied after the slab is cast and deck attachments and hanger clips are installed, so that later welding or drilling does not damage it; but if it comes too late, pipes and ducts already shield the beams and the spray gun cannot reach.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「表面準備、環境條件與施工順序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing\" is correct?","options":["只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。","被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。","被覆能否在火災時留在鋼材上，首先取決於施工當天的表面與環境：油汙、軋鋼鱗片、浮鏽或不相容的底漆會降低黏結，結露的鋼面會讓塗膜附著不良，低溫則使水泥系材料無法正常水化。"],"optionsEn":["If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection.","Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.","Whether protection stays on the steel in a fire depends first on the surface and ambient conditions on the day of application: oil, mill scale, loose rust or an incompatible primer reduce bond, condensation on the steel prevents coating adhesion, and low temperature stops cementitious products from hydrating properly."],"answer":2,"explanation":"被覆能否在火災時留在鋼材上，首先取決於施工當天的表面與環境：油汙、軋鋼鱗片、浮鏽或不相容的底漆會降低黏結，結露的鋼面會讓塗膜附著不良，低溫則使水泥系材料無法正常水化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Whether protection stays on the steel in a fire depends first on the surface and ambient conditions on the day of application: oil, mill scale, loose rust or an incompatible primer reduce bond, condensation on the steel prevents coating adhesion, and low temperature stops cementitious products from hydrating properly. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b093-v13-18","title":"表面準備、環境條件與施工順序：定量估算","titleEn":"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼材表面與環境條件」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Substrate and ambient conditions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Magnus 露點 Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ)，γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T)。氣溫 28°C、相對濕度 85%：γ = ln(0.85) + 17.62×28/271.12 ≈ 1.657，Td ≈ 243.12×1.657/15.96 ≈ 25.2°C；若要求鋼面高於露點 3°C，鋼面須 ≥ 28.2°C，量得 26°C 即不得塗裝。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Magnus dew point Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ), with γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T). At 28°C and 85% relative humidity, γ = ln(0.85) + 17.62×28/271.12 ≈ 1.657 and Td ≈ 243.12×1.657/15.96 ≈ 25.2°C; requiring steel at least 3°C above dew point means 28.2°C or more, so a measured 26°C stops coating. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每班開工前記錄氣溫、相對濕度、鋼面溫度與露點，檢查表面清潔度與底漆狀態，必要時先做小面積黏結試噴；SFRM 須確認基材溫度與通風符合廠商要求，並在施作前完成吊架、夾具與焊接的先行件檢查，簽核後才放行噴覆。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before each shift record air temperature, relative humidity, steel surface temperature and dew point, and inspect cleanliness and primer condition, with a small bond trial patch where needed; for SFRM confirm substrate temperature and ventilation meet the manufacturer's limits, and complete a pre-application check of hangers, clips and welding, released by signature before spraying begins.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Magnus 露點 Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ)，γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T)。氣溫 28°C、相對濕度 85%：γ = ln(0.85) + 17.62×28/271.12 ≈ 1.657，Td ≈ 243.12×1.657/15.96 ≈ 25.2°C；若要求鋼面高於露點 3°C，鋼面須 ≥ 28.2°C，量得 26°C 即不得塗裝。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Magnus dew point Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ), with γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T). At 28°C and 85% relative humidity, γ = ln(0.85) + 17.62×28/271.12 ≈ 1.657 and Td ≈ 243.12×1.657/15.96 ≈ 25.2°C; requiring steel at least 3°C above dew point means 28.2°C or more, so a measured 26°C stops coating. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「表面準備、環境條件與施工順序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing\", which statement holds?","options":["Magnus 露點 Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ)，γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T)。","約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。","既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。"],"optionsEn":["Magnus dew point Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ), with γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T).","A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used.","If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Magnus 露點 Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ)，γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Magnus dew point Td = 243.12·γ/(17.62 − γ), with γ = ln(RH) + 17.62·T/(243.12 + T). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b093-v13-19","title":"表面準備、環境條件與施工順序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼材表面與環境條件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Substrate and ambient conditions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每班開工前記錄氣溫、相對濕度、鋼面溫度與露點，檢查表面清潔度與底漆狀態，必要時先做小面積黏結試噴；SFRM 須確認基材溫度與通風符合廠商要求，並在施作前完成吊架、夾具與焊接的先行件檢查，簽核後才放行噴覆。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before each shift record air temperature, relative humidity, steel surface temperature and dew point, and inspect cleanliness and primer condition, with a small bond trial patch where needed; for SFRM confirm substrate temperature and ventilation meet the manufacturer's limits, and complete a pre-application check of hangers, clips and welding, released by signature before spraying begins. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把被覆前檢查設為停止點：鋼承板焊接、吊架夾具、剪力釘與穿孔全部完成，表面與環境紀錄合格後，由監造簽發被覆許可；之後任何焊接或鑽孔都要事先申請，並排定補修與複驗。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make the pre-fireproofing inspection a hold point: deck welding, hanger clips, shear studs and penetrations all complete and surface and ambient records accepted, then the supervising engineer issues a permit to fireproof; any later welding or drilling requires a prior request and scheduled repair and re-inspection.","failure":"注意干擾：在潮濕清晨噴塗膨脹漆，膜下結露造成大面積起泡剝離；SFRM 噴在帶油的鋼梁上，乾燥後看似完整，卻在後續振動或碰撞時整塊脫落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Intumescent sprayed on a damp morning with condensation under the film blisters and peels over large areas; SFRM sprayed on oily beams looks intact once dry but falls off in sheets under later vibration or impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每班開工前記錄氣溫、相對濕度、鋼面溫度與露點，檢查表面清潔度與底漆狀態，必要時先做小面積黏結試噴；SFRM 須確認基材溫度與通風符合廠商要求，並在施作前完成吊架、夾具與焊接的先行件檢查，簽核後才放行噴覆。","textEn":"Before each shift record air temperature, relative humidity, steel surface temperature and dew point, and inspect cleanliness and primer condition, with a small bond trial patch where needed; for SFRM confirm substrate temperature and ventilation meet the manufacturer's limits, and complete a pre-application check of hangers, clips and welding, released by signature before spraying begins.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把被覆前檢查設為停止點：鋼承板焊接、吊架夾具、剪力釘與穿孔全部完成，表面與環境紀錄合格後，由監造簽發被覆許可；之後任何焊接或鑽孔都要事先申請，並排定補修與複驗。","textEn":"Make the pre-fireproofing inspection a hold point: deck welding, hanger clips, shear studs and penetrations all complete and surface and ambient records accepted, then the supervising engineer issues a permit to fireproof; any later welding or drilling requires a prior request and scheduled repair and re-inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「表面準備、環境條件與施工順序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","每班開工前記錄氣溫、相對濕度、鋼面溫度與露點，檢查表面清潔度與底漆狀態，必要時先做小面積黏結試噴。","被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before each shift record air temperature, relative humidity, steel surface temperature and dew point, and inspect cleanliness and primer condition, with a small bond trial patch where needed.","Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每班開工前記錄氣溫、相對濕度、鋼面溫度與露點，檢查表面清潔度與底漆狀態，必要時先做小面積黏結試噴；SFRM 須確認基材溫度與通風符合廠商要求，並在施作前完成吊架、夾具與焊接的先行件檢查，簽核後才放行噴覆。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before each shift record air temperature, relative humidity, steel surface temperature and dew point, and inspect cleanliness and primer condition, with a small bond trial patch where needed; for SFRM confirm substrate temperature and ventilation meet the manufacturer's limits, and complete a pre-application check of hangers, clips and welding, released by signature before spraying begins. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b093-v13-20","title":"表面準備、環境條件與施工順序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼材表面與環境條件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Substrate and ambient conditions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在潮濕清晨噴塗膨脹漆，膜下結露造成大面積起泡剝離；SFRM 噴在帶油的鋼梁上，乾燥後看似完整，卻在後續振動或碰撞時整塊脫落。若被覆完成後才在梁上焊接吊架，熱影響區的被覆燒損又常被天花板遮住而未被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Intumescent sprayed on a damp morning with condensation under the film blisters and peels over large areas; SFRM sprayed on oily beams looks intact once dry but falls off in sheets under later vibration or impact. Hangers welded to beams after fireproofing burn the protection in the heat-affected zone, and the damage is often hidden by the ceiling and never found. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：施工順序因此是品質的一部分，而不只是進度問題。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sequencing is therefore part of quality, not just of programme.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在潮濕清晨噴塗膨脹漆，膜下結露造成大面積起泡剝離；SFRM 噴在帶油的鋼梁上，乾燥後看似完整，卻在後續振動或碰撞時整塊脫落。若被覆完成後才在梁上焊接吊架，熱影響區的被覆燒損又常被天花板遮住而未被發現。","textEn":"Intumescent sprayed on a damp morning with condensation under the film blisters and peels over large areas; SFRM sprayed on oily beams looks intact once dry but falls off in sheets under later vibration or impact. Hangers welded to beams after fireproofing burn the protection in the heat-affected zone, and the damage is often hidden by the ceiling and never found.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面準備、環境條件與施工順序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Surface preparation, ambient conditions and sequencing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。","在潮濕清晨噴塗膨脹漆，膜下結露造成大面積起泡剝離；SFRM 噴在帶油的鋼梁上，乾燥後看似完整，卻在後續振動或碰撞時整塊脫落。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.","Intumescent sprayed on a damp morning with condensation under the film blisters and peels over large areas."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在潮濕清晨噴塗膨脹漆，膜下結露造成大面積起泡剝離；SFRM 噴在帶油的鋼梁上，乾燥後看似完整，卻在後續振動或碰撞時整塊脫落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Intumescent sprayed on a damp morning with condensation under the film blisters and peels over large areas; SFRM sprayed on oily beams looks intact once dry but falls off in sheets under later vibration or impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b093-v13-21","title":"交叉作業損傷與等效厚度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Trade damage and equivalent thickness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「機電吊架與補修區」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hanger penetrations and patch areas” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"被覆完成後，機電、消防灑水、天花板與帷幕牆工班仍需在鋼梁上固定吊架、切割或搬運材料，常刮除或撞落局部被覆。由於熱流近似與厚度成反比，局部變薄或裸露的區域就是熱的捷徑，使該處鋼材升溫遠快於平均厚度所預測。NIST 在世界貿易中心調查中以「熱等效均勻厚度」描述不均勻被覆的實際效果：原設計的平均厚度並不能代表最薄處的風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「機電吊架與補修區」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After fireproofing, MEP, sprinkler, ceiling and façade trades still fix hangers to beams and cut or move materials, often scraping or knocking off local patches. Because heat flow is roughly inversely proportional to thickness, thin or bare spots become thermal short cuts where the steel heats much faster than the average thickness predicts. In its World Trade Center investigation NIST described the real effect of uneven protection with a thermally equivalent uniform thickness: the average thickness does not represent the risk at the thinnest areas. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Hanger penetrations and patch areas” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：並聯熱流路徑的等效厚度 d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For parallel heat paths the equivalent thickness is d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ).","failure":"常見誤解：「被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「機電吊架與補修區」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Hanger penetrations and patch areas”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-21-k1","title":"交叉作業損傷與等效厚度","titleEn":"Trade damage and equivalent thickness","text":"被覆完成後，機電、消防灑水、天花板與帷幕牆工班仍需在鋼梁上固定吊架、切割或搬運材料，常刮除或撞落局部被覆。由於熱流近似與厚度成反比，局部變薄或裸露的區域就是熱的捷徑，使該處鋼材升溫遠快於平均厚度所預測。","textEn":"After fireproofing, MEP, sprinkler, ceiling and façade trades still fix hangers to beams and cut or move materials, often scraping or knocking off local patches. Because heat flow is roughly inversely proportional to thickness, thin or bare spots become thermal short cuts where the steel heats much faster than the average thickness predicts.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交叉作業損傷與等效厚度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Trade damage and equivalent thickness\" is correct?","options":["被覆完成後，機電、消防灑水、天花板與帷幕牆工班仍需在鋼梁上固定吊架、切割或搬運材料，常刮除或撞落局部被覆。","被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。","平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。"],"optionsEn":["After fireproofing, MEP, sprinkler, ceiling and façade trades still fix hangers to beams and cut or move materials, often scraping or knocking off local patches.","Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.","If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"被覆完成後，機電、消防灑水、天花板與帷幕牆工班仍需在鋼梁上固定吊架、切割或搬運材料，常刮除或撞落局部被覆。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After fireproofing, MEP, sprinkler, ceiling and façade trades still fix hangers to beams and cut or move materials, often scraping or knocking off local patches. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b093-v13-22","title":"交叉作業損傷與等效厚度：定量估算","titleEn":"Trade damage and equivalent thickness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「機電吊架與補修區」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hanger penetrations and patch areas” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：並聯熱流路徑的等效厚度 d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ)。90% 面積 25 mm、10% 面積因刮損只剩 5 mm：d_eq = 1/(0.9/25 + 0.1/5) = 1/0.056 ≈ 17.9 mm，算術平均卻是 23 mm；升溫率約為原設計的 25/17.9 ≈ 1.4 倍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For parallel heat paths the equivalent thickness is d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ). With 90% of the area at 25 mm and 10% scraped to 5 mm: d_eq = 1/(0.9/25 + 0.1/5) = 1/0.056 ≈ 17.9 mm, although the arithmetic mean is 23 mm; the heating rate rises to about 25/17.9 ≈ 1.4 times the design value. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：天花板封板前安排第二次全面目視與抽量，特別檢查吊架、穿孔與梁柱接頭周邊；補修使用原產品或廠商核可的補修材料，補修區重新量測厚度並拍照，記入樓層補修清單後才准許封板。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Schedule a second full visual inspection with spot measurements before ceilings close, focusing on hangers, penetrations and beam–column joints; repairs use the original product or a manufacturer-approved patching material, each repaired area is re-measured and photographed, and the floor's repair log must be complete before ceilings may be closed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"並聯熱流路徑的等效厚度 d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ)。90% 面積 25 mm、10% 面積因刮損只剩 5 mm：d_eq = 1/(0.9/25 + 0.1/5) = 1/0.056 ≈ 17.9 mm，算術平均卻是 23 mm；升溫率約為原設計的 25/17.9 ≈ 1.4 倍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For parallel heat paths the equivalent thickness is d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ). With 90% of the area at 25 mm and 10% scraped to 5 mm: d_eq = 1/(0.9/25 + 0.1/5) = 1/0.056 ≈ 17.9 mm, although the arithmetic mean is 23 mm; the heating rate rises to about 25/17.9 ≈ 1.4 times the design value. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「交叉作業損傷與等效厚度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Trade damage and equivalent thickness\", which statement holds?","options":["防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。","並聯熱流路徑的等效厚度 d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ)。","鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。"],"optionsEn":["Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.","For parallel heat paths the equivalent thickness is d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ).","Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame."],"answer":1,"explanation":"並聯熱流路徑的等效厚度 d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For parallel heat paths the equivalent thickness is d_eq = 1/Σ(fᵢ/dᵢ). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b093-v13-23","title":"交叉作業損傷與等效厚度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Trade damage and equivalent thickness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「機電吊架與補修區」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hanger penetrations and patch areas” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"天花板封板前安排第二次全面目視與抽量，特別檢查吊架、穿孔與梁柱接頭周邊；補修使用原產品或廠商核可的補修材料，補修區重新量測厚度並拍照，記入樓層補修清單後才准許封板。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Schedule a second full visual inspection with spot measurements before ceilings close, focusing on hangers, penetrations and beam–column joints; repairs use the original product or a manufacturer-approved patching material, each repaired area is re-measured and photographed, and the floor's repair log must be complete before ceilings may be closed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合約應規定誰破壞誰負擔、由原被覆廠商修補，並要求機電吊架優先採用夾具而非焊接；每層樓在天花板封閉前設最終被覆檢查停止點，由監造與第三方檢驗員共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The contract should make the trade that causes damage pay for repair by the original fireproofing contractor and require clamp-on rather than welded MEP hangers; each floor gets a final fireproofing hold point before ceilings close, signed jointly by the supervising engineer and the third-party inspector.","failure":"注意干擾：天花板封閉後才發現被覆缺損，修補成本極高而常被忽略；火災時這些裸露點附近的梁下翼板先達臨界溫度，造成局部撓曲與接頭破壞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Damage found only after ceilings close is so expensive to reach that it is often ignored; in a fire the bottom flange near these bare spots reaches its critical temperature first, causing local deflection and connection failure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"天花板封板前安排第二次全面目視與抽量，特別檢查吊架、穿孔與梁柱接頭周邊；補修使用原產品或廠商核可的補修材料，補修區重新量測厚度並拍照，記入樓層補修清單後才准許封板。","textEn":"Schedule a second full visual inspection with spot measurements before ceilings close, focusing on hangers, penetrations and beam–column joints; repairs use the original product or a manufacturer-approved patching material, each repaired area is re-measured and photographed, and the floor's repair log must be complete before ceilings may be closed.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合約應規定誰破壞誰負擔、由原被覆廠商修補，並要求機電吊架優先採用夾具而非焊接；每層樓在天花板封閉前設最終被覆檢查停止點，由監造與第三方檢驗員共同簽認。","textEn":"The contract should make the trade that causes damage pay for repair by the original fireproofing contractor and require clamp-on rather than welded MEP hangers; each floor gets a final fireproofing hold point before ceilings close, signed jointly by the supervising engineer and the third-party inspector.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「交叉作業損傷與等效厚度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Trade damage and equivalent thickness\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。","天花板封板前安排第二次全面目視與抽量，特別檢查吊架、穿孔與梁柱接頭周邊。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.","Schedule a second full visual inspection with spot measurements before ceilings close, focusing on hangers, penetrations and beam–column joints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"天花板封板前安排第二次全面目視與抽量，特別檢查吊架、穿孔與梁柱接頭周邊；補修使用原產品或廠商核可的補修材料，補修區重新量測厚度並拍照，記入樓層補修清單後才准許封板。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Schedule a second full visual inspection with spot measurements before ceilings close, focusing on hangers, penetrations and beam–column joints; repairs use the original product or a manufacturer-approved patching material, each repaired area is re-measured and photographed, and the floor's repair log must be complete before ceilings may be closed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b093-v13-24","title":"交叉作業損傷與等效厚度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Trade damage and equivalent thickness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「機電吊架與補修區」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hanger penetrations and patch areas” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"天花板封閉後才發現被覆缺損，修補成本極高而常被忽略；火災時這些裸露點附近的梁下翼板先達臨界溫度，造成局部撓曲與接頭破壞。NIST 的世界貿易中心調查也指出，飛機撞擊使樓板桁架與柱上的被覆大量脫落，是鋼構件快速升溫的重要原因。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Damage found only after ceilings close is so expensive to reach that it is often ignored; in a fire the bottom flange near these bare spots reaches its critical temperature first, causing local deflection and connection failure. NIST's World Trade Center investigation also found that the aircraft impacts dislodged much of the fireproofing on floor trusses and columns, a key reason for rapid heating of the steel. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：NIST 在世界貿易中心調查中以「熱等效均勻厚度」描述不均勻被覆的實際效果：原設計的平均厚度並不能代表最薄處的風險。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In its World Trade Center investigation NIST described the real effect of uneven protection with a thermally equivalent uniform thickness: the average thickness does not represent the risk at the thinnest areas.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"天花板封閉後才發現被覆缺損，修補成本極高而常被忽略；火災時這些裸露點附近的梁下翼板先達臨界溫度，造成局部撓曲與接頭破壞。NIST 的世界貿易中心調查也指出，飛機撞擊使樓板桁架與柱上的被覆大量脫落，是鋼構件快速升溫的重要原因。","textEn":"Damage found only after ceilings close is so expensive to reach that it is often ignored; in a fire the bottom flange near these bare spots reaches its critical temperature first, causing local deflection and connection failure. NIST's World Trade Center investigation also found that the aircraft impacts dislodged much of the fireproofing on floor trusses and columns, a key reason for rapid heating of the steel.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「交叉作業損傷與等效厚度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Trade damage and equivalent thickness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["天花板封閉後才發現被覆缺損，修補成本極高而常被忽略；火災時這些裸露點附近的梁下翼板先達臨界溫度，造成局部撓曲與接頭破壞。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。"],"optionsEn":["Damage found only after ceilings close is so expensive to reach that it is often ignored.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"天花板封閉後才發現被覆缺損，修補成本極高而常被忽略；火災時這些裸露點附近的梁下翼板先達臨界溫度，造成局部撓曲與接頭破壞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Damage found only after ceilings close is so expensive to reach that it is often ignored; in a fire the bottom flange near these bare spots reaches its critical temperature first, causing local deflection and connection failure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b093-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗」與「標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength\" and \"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b093-v13-25","title":"現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「厚度、密度與黏結抽驗」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thickness, density and bond sampling” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"現場驗收把試驗室的耐火設計轉成三個可量測的量：厚度、密度與黏結強度。厚度依 ASTM E605 以探針式量規在指定位置量測，梁與柱都有規定的點數與抽樣比例；密度由切取試塊的體積與乾重求得；黏結強度則依 ASTM E736 以拉拔試驗確認被覆不會從鋼材或自身內部分離。美國 IBC 要求這些項目由特別檢驗員執行，並依樓高提高高層建築的黏結強度門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「厚度、密度與黏結抽驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Field acceptance turns the laboratory fire design into three measurable quantities: thickness, density and bond strength. Thickness is measured to ASTM E605 with a probe gauge at prescribed locations, with set numbers of readings and sampling rates for beams and columns; density comes from the volume and dry mass of cut samples; and bond strength is checked to ASTM E736 with a pull-off test showing that the material does not separate from the steel or within itself. The US IBC assigns these items to a special inspector and raises the bond threshold for high-rise buildings by height. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Thickness, density and bond sampling” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：IBC 黏結門檻換算：150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa；430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa；1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: IBC bond thresholds: 150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa; 430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa; 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「厚度、密度與黏結抽驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Thickness, density and bond sampling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-25-k1","title":"現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗","titleEn":"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength","text":"現場驗收把試驗室的耐火設計轉成三個可量測的量：厚度、密度與黏結強度。厚度依 ASTM E605 以探針式量規在指定位置量測，梁與柱都有規定的點數與抽樣比例；密度由切取試塊的體積與乾重求得；黏結強度則依 ASTM E736 以拉拔試驗確認被覆不會從鋼材或自身內部分離。","textEn":"Field acceptance turns the laboratory fire design into three measurable quantities: thickness, density and bond strength. Thickness is measured to ASTM E605 with a probe gauge at prescribed locations, with set numbers of readings and sampling rates for beams and columns; density comes from the volume and dry mass of cut samples; and bond strength is checked to ASTM E736 with a pull-off test showing that the material does not separate from the steel or within itself.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength\" is correct?","options":["平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。","現場驗收把試驗室的耐火設計轉成三個可量測的量：厚度、密度與黏結強度。","約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。"],"optionsEn":["If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected.","Field acceptance turns the laboratory fire design into three measurable quantities: thickness, density and bond strength.","A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used."],"answer":1,"explanation":"現場驗收把試驗室的耐火設計轉成三個可量測的量：厚度、密度與黏結強度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Field acceptance turns the laboratory fire design into three measurable quantities: thickness, density and bond strength. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b093-v13-26","title":"現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「厚度、密度與黏結抽驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thickness, density and bond sampling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：IBC 黏結門檻換算：150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa；430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa；1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa。若拉拔蓋接觸面積 A = 0.0045 m²，所需破壞荷重 F = σ·A 分別約 32 N、93 N 與 215 N。密度試塊 0.30×0.30×0.025 m = 0.00225 m³、乾重 0.63 kg，密度 = 280 kg/m³。門檻為 IBC 規定，其餘為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: IBC bond thresholds: 150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa; 430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa; 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa. With a pull-off cap area A = 0.0045 m², the required failure loads F = σ·A are about 32 N, 93 N and 215 N. A density sample of 0.30×0.30×0.025 m = 0.00225 m³ with 0.63 kg dry mass gives 280 kg/m³. The thresholds are IBC values; the rest are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依 IBC 第 1705 節抽樣：樓板每 1,000 ft² 至少 4 點厚度；每層至少 25% 構件，梁在 12 in 長度兩端各量 9 點、寬翼柱各量 12 點；密度與黏結每 2,500 ft² 至少一組。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample per IBC Section 1705: at least 4 thickness readings per 1,000 ft² of floor; at least 25% of members per storey, with 9 readings at each end of a 12 in length on beams and 12 on wide-flange columns; at least one density and one bond sample per 2,500 ft².","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"IBC 黏結門檻換算：150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa；430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa；1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa。若拉拔蓋接觸面積 A = 0.0045 m²，所需破壞荷重 F = σ·A 分別約 32 N、93 N 與 215 N。密度試塊 0.30×0.30×0.025 m = 0.00225 m³、乾重 0.63 kg，密度 = 280 kg/m³。門檻為 IBC 規定，其餘為教學假設。","textEn":"IBC bond thresholds: 150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa; 430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa; 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa. With a pull-off cap area A = 0.0045 m², the required failure loads F = σ·A are about 32 N, 93 N and 215 N. A density sample of 0.30×0.30×0.025 m = 0.00225 m³ with 0.63 kg dry mass gives 280 kg/m³. The thresholds are IBC values; the rest are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength\", which statement holds?","options":["既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。","被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。","IBC 黏結門檻換算：150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating.","Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section.","IBC bond thresholds: 150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa; 430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa; 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"IBC 黏結門檻換算：150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa；430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa；1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"IBC bond thresholds: 150 psf × 47.88 Pa/psf ≈ 7.2 kPa; 430 psf ≈ 20.6 kPa; 1,000 psf ≈ 47.9 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b093-v13-27","title":"現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「厚度、密度與黏結抽驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thickness, density and bond sampling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依 IBC 第 1705 節抽樣：樓板每 1,000 ft² 至少 4 點厚度；每層至少 25% 構件，梁在 12 in 長度兩端各量 9 點、寬翼柱各量 12 點；密度與黏結每 2,500 ft² 至少一組。平均厚度須達設計值；設計 ≥ 1 in 時單點不得低於設計值減 1/4 in，小於 1 in 時不得低於設計值減 25%。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample per IBC Section 1705: at least 4 thickness readings per 1,000 ft² of floor; at least 25% of members per storey, with 9 readings at each end of a 12 in length on beams and 12 on wide-flange columns; at least one density and one bond sample per 2,500 ft². Mean thickness must reach the design value; for a design of 1 in or more no reading may fall below design minus 1/4 in, and below 1 in no reading may fall below design minus 25%. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：檢驗計畫須在施工前送審，列明抽樣位置的隨機選取方式（不由施工者指定）、量規校正、取樣孔的補修方法，以及不合格時擴大抽樣的規則；高層建築要先確認適用的黏結強度門檻。","observationEn":"Site practice: Submit the inspection plan before work starts, stating how sample locations are chosen at random rather than by the applicator, gauge calibration, how sample holes are patched and the rule for expanding sampling after a failure; for high-rise buildings confirm the applicable bond threshold first.","failure":"注意干擾：只量容易到達的腹板而不量下翼板邊緣，或讓遠超設計的讀值拉高平均，都會掩蓋薄點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measuring only the easily reached web and not the bottom-flange edges, or letting very thick readings inflate the average, hides thin spots. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依 IBC 第 1705 節抽樣：樓板每 1,000 ft² 至少 4 點厚度；每層至少 25% 構件，梁在 12 in 長度兩端各量 9 點、寬翼柱各量 12 點；密度與黏結每 2,500 ft² 至少一組。平均厚度須達設計值；設計 ≥ 1 in 時單點不得低於設計值減 1/4 in，小於 1 in 時不得低於設計值減 25%。","textEn":"Sample per IBC Section 1705: at least 4 thickness readings per 1,000 ft² of floor; at least 25% of members per storey, with 9 readings at each end of a 12 in length on beams and 12 on wide-flange columns; at least one density and one bond sample per 2,500 ft². Mean thickness must reach the design value; for a design of 1 in or more no reading may fall below design minus 1/4 in, and below 1 in no reading may fall below design minus 25%.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"檢驗計畫須在施工前送審，列明抽樣位置的隨機選取方式（不由施工者指定）、量規校正、取樣孔的補修方法，以及不合格時擴大抽樣的規則；高層建築要先確認適用的黏結強度門檻。","textEn":"Submit the inspection plan before work starts, stating how sample locations are chosen at random rather than by the applicator, gauge calibration, how sample holes are patched and the rule for expanding sampling after a failure; for high-rise buildings confirm the applicable bond threshold first.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength\"?","options":["依 IBC 第 1705 節抽樣：樓板每 1,000 ft² 至少 4 點厚度。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。"],"optionsEn":["Sample per IBC Section 1705: at least 4 thickness readings per 1,000 ft² of floor.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依 IBC 第 1705 節抽樣：樓板每 1,000 ft² 至少 4 點厚度；每層至少 25% 構件，梁在 12 in 長度兩端各量 9 點、寬翼柱各量 12 點；密度與黏結每 2,500 ft² 至少一組。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample per IBC Section 1705: at least 4 thickness readings per 1,000 ft² of floor; at least 25% of members per storey, with 9 readings at each end of a 12 in length on beams and 12 on wide-flange columns; at least one density and one bond sample per 2,500 ft². Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b093-v13-28","title":"現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「厚度、密度與黏結抽驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thickness, density and bond sampling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量容易到達的腹板而不量下翼板邊緣，或讓遠超設計的讀值拉高平均，都會掩蓋薄點。世界貿易中心樓板桁架原規定 1/2 in，NIST 引用的實測平均約 0.75 in、變異係數約 0.4；若以常態分布估算，約兩成讀值可能低於 0.5 in。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measuring only the easily reached web and not the bottom-flange edges, or letting very thick readings inflate the average, hides thin spots. The World Trade Center floor trusses originally specified 1/2 in, and NIST cited a measured average of about 0.75 in with a coefficient of variation of about 0.4; a normal-distribution estimate puts about one reading in five below 0.5 in. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：美國 IBC 要求這些項目由特別檢驗員執行，並依樓高提高高層建築的黏結強度門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The US IBC assigns these items to a special inspector and raises the bond threshold for high-rise buildings by height.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量容易到達的腹板而不量下翼板邊緣，或讓遠超設計的讀值拉高平均，都會掩蓋薄點。世界貿易中心樓板桁架原規定 1/2 in，NIST 引用的實測平均約 0.75 in、變異係數約 0.4；若以常態分布估算，約兩成讀值可能低於 0.5 in。","textEn":"Measuring only the easily reached web and not the bottom-flange edges, or letting very thick readings inflate the average, hides thin spots. The World Trade Center floor trusses originally specified 1/2 in, and NIST cited a measured average of about 0.75 in with a coefficient of variation of about 0.4; a normal-distribution estimate puts about one reading in five below 0.5 in.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「現場厚度、密度與黏結強度抽驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Field sampling of thickness, density and bond strength\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只量容易到達的腹板而不量下翼板邊緣，或讓遠超設計的讀值拉高平均，都會掩蓋薄點。","約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Measuring only the easily reached web and not the bottom-flange edges, or letting very thick readings inflate the average, hides thin spots.","A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只量容易到達的腹板而不量下翼板邊緣，或讓遠超設計的讀值拉高平均，都會掩蓋薄點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measuring only the easily reached web and not the bottom-flange edges, or letting very thick readings inflate the average, hides thin spots. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b093-v13-29","title":"標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「耐火試驗登錄與約束條件」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fire-test listing and restraint” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"ASTM E119（與 UL 263 同等）以標準升溫曲線加熱載重試體，梁的溫度判準為四點平均 593°C 或任一點 704°C；試驗結果以登錄設計公告，規定鋼材斷面、被覆產品、厚度與構造細部。試驗分為約束與非約束兩種等級：約束假設周邊結構阻止梁受熱伸長，會在梁內產生軸壓並改變破壞模式。實際建築的約束程度介於兩者之間，熱膨脹推擠柱與接頭本身也是火災倒塌的重要機制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「耐火試驗登錄與約束條件」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"ASTM E119, equivalent to UL 263, heats loaded specimens along a standard time–temperature curve; for beams the temperature criteria are 593°C averaged over four thermocouples or 704°C at any point. Results are published as listed designs that fix the steel section, protection product, thickness and construction details. Tests yield restrained and unrestrained ratings: restraint assumes the surrounding structure prevents thermal elongation of the beam, inducing axial compression and changing the failure mode. Real buildings fall between the two, and thermal expansion pushing on columns and connections is itself an important collapse mechanism. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fire-test listing and restraint” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：受熱伸長 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Thermal elongation ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","failure":"常見誤解：「約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「耐火試驗登錄與約束條件」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fire-test listing and restraint”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-29-k1","title":"標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類","titleEn":"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification","text":"ASTM E119（與 UL 263 同等）以標準升溫曲線加熱載重試體，梁的溫度判準為四點平均 593°C 或任一點 704°C；試驗結果以登錄設計公告，規定鋼材斷面、被覆產品、厚度與構造細部。試驗分為約束與非約束兩種等級：約束假設周邊結構阻止梁受熱伸長，會在梁內產生軸壓並改變破壞模式。","textEn":"ASTM E119, equivalent to UL 263, heats loaded specimens along a standard time–temperature curve; for beams the temperature criteria are 593°C averaged over four thermocouples or 704°C at any point. Results are published as listed designs that fix the steel section, protection product, thickness and construction details.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification\" is correct?","options":["約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。","防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。","ASTM E119（與 UL 263 同等）以標準升溫曲線加熱載重試體，梁的溫度判準為四點平均 593°C 或任一點 704°C。"],"optionsEn":["A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used.","Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.","ASTM E119, equivalent to UL 263, heats loaded specimens along a standard time–temperature curve."],"answer":2,"explanation":"ASTM E119（與 UL 263 同等）以標準升溫曲線加熱載重試體，梁的溫度判準為四點平均 593°C 或任一點 704°C；試驗結果以登錄設計公告，規定鋼材斷面、被覆產品、厚度與構造細部。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"ASTM E119, equivalent to UL 263, heats loaded specimens along a standard time–temperature curve; for beams the temperature criteria are 593°C averaged over four thermocouples or 704°C at any point. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b093-v13-30","title":"標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類：定量估算","titleEn":"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「耐火試驗登錄與約束條件」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fire-test listing and restraint” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：受熱伸長 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /K、跨度 L = 10.67 m（35 ft）、升溫 ΔT = 500 K：ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×10.67×500 ≈ 64 mm。若完全約束，σ = E·α·ΔT = 200,000×1.2×10⁻⁵×500 = 1,200 MPa，遠超過降伏強度，代表實際上必有接頭滑移、梁挫屈或柱被推出。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Thermal elongation ΔL = α·L·ΔT. With α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /K, span L = 10.67 m (35 ft) and ΔT = 500 K: ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×10.67×500 ≈ 64 mm. If fully restrained, σ = E·α·ΔT = 200,000×1.2×10⁻⁵×500 = 1,200 MPa, far beyond yield, so in reality connections slip, the beam buckles or the column is pushed out. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：審查送審資料時逐項比對登錄設計：鋼材斷面範圍、樓板種類、被覆產品與厚度、是否需金屬網或黏結劑，以及採用約束或非約束等級；建築的約束分類須由結構設計者依周邊構架判定並寫入圖說，而非由被覆廠商自行選擇。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: When reviewing submittals compare item by item with the listed design: steel section range, slab type, protection product and thickness, need for mesh or bonding agent, and whether the restrained or unrestrained rating is used; the restraint classification must be decided by the structural engineer from the surrounding framing and written on the drawings, not chosen by the applicator.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"受熱伸長 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /K、跨度 L = 10.67 m（35 ft）、升溫 ΔT = 500 K：ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×10.67×500 ≈ 64 mm。若完全約束，σ = E·α·ΔT = 200,000×1.2×10⁻⁵×500 = 1,200 MPa，遠超過降伏強度，代表實際上必有接頭滑移、梁挫屈或柱被推出。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Thermal elongation ΔL = α·L·ΔT. With α = 1.2×10⁻⁵ /K, span L = 10.67 m (35 ft) and ΔT = 500 K: ΔL = 1.2×10⁻⁵×10.67×500 ≈ 64 mm. If fully restrained, σ = E·α·ΔT = 200,000×1.2×10⁻⁵×500 = 1,200 MPa, far beyond yield, so in reality connections slip, the beam buckles or the column is pushed out. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification\", which statement holds?","options":["受熱伸長 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。","鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。","噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal elongation ΔL = α·L·ΔT.","Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame.","Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location."],"answer":0,"explanation":"受熱伸長 ΔL = α·L·ΔT。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Thermal elongation ΔL = α·L·ΔT. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b093-v13-31","title":"標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「耐火試驗登錄與約束條件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fire-test listing and restraint” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"審查送審資料時逐項比對登錄設計：鋼材斷面範圍、樓板種類、被覆產品與厚度、是否需金屬網或黏結劑，以及採用約束或非約束等級；建築的約束分類須由結構設計者依周邊構架判定並寫入圖說，而非由被覆廠商自行選擇。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"When reviewing submittals compare item by item with the listed design: steel section range, slab type, protection product and thickness, need for mesh or bonding agent, and whether the restrained or unrestrained rating is used; the restraint classification must be decided by the structural engineer from the surrounding framing and written on the drawings, not chosen by the applicator. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：圖說應明確標示採用的試驗登錄編號與約束條件；任何偏離登錄的構造（不同樓板、不同斷面、開孔梁）都要取得試驗機構或廠商的工程判定，並經防火設計者與主管建築機關認可後才可施工。","observationEn":"Site practice: Drawings must state the listing number and restraint condition used; any construction that departs from the listing, such as a different slab, section or a cellular beam, needs an engineering judgement from the test body or manufacturer, accepted by the fire designer and the building authority before work proceeds.","failure":"注意干擾：NIST 委託 UL 對世界貿易中心樓板桁架做的 ASTM E119 試驗中，35 ft 跨度非約束試體得到 2 小時，約束試體只有 1.5 小時，與一般預期相反，提醒工程師小型試驗爐的結果不能直接外推到長跨度與真實約束。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: In the ASTM E119 tests of World Trade Center floor trusses that NIST commissioned from UL, the 35 ft unrestrained specimen achieved 2 hours while the restrained one achieved only 1.5 hours, contrary to expectation, a reminder that small-furnace results cannot simply be extrapolated to long spans and real restraint. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"審查送審資料時逐項比對登錄設計：鋼材斷面範圍、樓板種類、被覆產品與厚度、是否需金屬網或黏結劑，以及採用約束或非約束等級；建築的約束分類須由結構設計者依周邊構架判定並寫入圖說，而非由被覆廠商自行選擇。","textEn":"When reviewing submittals compare item by item with the listed design: steel section range, slab type, protection product and thickness, need for mesh or bonding agent, and whether the restrained or unrestrained rating is used; the restraint classification must be decided by the structural engineer from the surrounding framing and written on the drawings, not chosen by the applicator.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"圖說應明確標示採用的試驗登錄編號與約束條件；任何偏離登錄的構造（不同樓板、不同斷面、開孔梁）都要取得試驗機構或廠商的工程判定，並經防火設計者與主管建築機關認可後才可施工。","textEn":"Drawings must state the listing number and restraint condition used; any construction that departs from the listing, such as a different slab, section or a cellular beam, needs an engineering judgement from the test body or manufacturer, accepted by the fire designer and the building authority before work proceeds.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","審查送審資料時逐項比對登錄設計：鋼材斷面範圍、樓板種類、被覆產品與厚度、是否需金屬網或黏結劑，以及採用約束或非約束等級。","只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","When reviewing submittals compare item by item with the listed design: steel section range, slab type, protection product and thickness, need for mesh or bonding agent, and whether the restrained or unrestrained rating is used.","If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection."],"answer":1,"explanation":"審查送審資料時逐項比對登錄設計：鋼材斷面範圍、樓板種類、被覆產品與厚度、是否需金屬網或黏結劑，以及採用約束或非約束等級；建築的約束分類須由結構設計者依周邊構架判定並寫入圖說，而非由被覆廠商自行選擇。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"When reviewing submittals compare item by item with the listed design: steel section range, slab type, protection product and thickness, need for mesh or bonding agent, and whether the restrained or unrestrained rating is used; the restraint classification must be decided by the structural engineer from the surrounding framing and written on the drawings, not chosen by the applicator. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b093-v13-32","title":"標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類：失效診斷","titleEn":"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「耐火試驗登錄與約束條件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fire-test listing and restraint” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"NIST 委託 UL 對世界貿易中心樓板桁架做的 ASTM E119 試驗中，35 ft 跨度非約束試體得到 2 小時，約束試體只有 1.5 小時，與一般預期相反，提醒工程師小型試驗爐的結果不能直接外推到長跨度與真實約束。忽略熱膨脹，柱與接頭可能在梁尚未失去強度前就被推壞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"In the ASTM E119 tests of World Trade Center floor trusses that NIST commissioned from UL, the 35 ft unrestrained specimen achieved 2 hours while the restrained one achieved only 1.5 hours, contrary to expectation, a reminder that small-furnace results cannot simply be extrapolated to long spans and real restraint. Ignoring thermal expansion lets columns and connections be pushed to failure before the beam itself loses strength. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：實際建築的約束程度介於兩者之間，熱膨脹推擠柱與接頭本身也是火災倒塌的重要機制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Real buildings fall between the two, and thermal expansion pushing on columns and connections is itself an important collapse mechanism.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「約束等級的耐火時效一定比非約束等級長，所以都應採用約束等級。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A restrained rating always lasts longer than an unrestrained one, so it should always be used.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"NIST 委託 UL 對世界貿易中心樓板桁架做的 ASTM E119 試驗中，35 ft 跨度非約束試體得到 2 小時，約束試體只有 1.5 小時，與一般預期相反，提醒工程師小型試驗爐的結果不能直接外推到長跨度與真實約束。忽略熱膨脹，柱與接頭可能在梁尚未失去強度前就被推壞。","textEn":"In the ASTM E119 tests of World Trade Center floor trusses that NIST commissioned from UL, the 35 ft unrestrained specimen achieved 2 hours while the restrained one achieved only 1.5 hours, contrary to expectation, a reminder that small-furnace results cannot simply be extrapolated to long spans and real restraint. Ignoring thermal expansion lets columns and connections be pushed to failure before the beam itself loses strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「標準耐火試驗、登錄設計與約束分類」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Standard fire tests, listed designs and restraint classification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。","NIST 委託 UL 對世界貿易中心樓板桁架做的 ASTM E119 試驗中，35 ft 跨度非約束試體得到 2 小時，約束試體只有 1.5 小時，與一般預期相反，提醒工程師小型試驗爐的結果不能直接外推到長跨度與真實約束。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.","In the ASTM E119 tests of World Trade Center floor trusses that NIST commissioned from UL, the 35 ft unrestrained specimen achieved 2 hours while the restrained one achieved only 1.5 hours, contrary to expectation, a reminder that small-furnace results cannot simply be extrapolated to long spans and real restraint."],"answer":2,"explanation":"NIST 委託 UL 對世界貿易中心樓板桁架做的 ASTM E119 試驗中，35 ft 跨度非約束試體得到 2 小時，約束試體只有 1.5 小時，與一般預期相反，提醒工程師小型試驗爐的結果不能直接外推到長跨度與真實約束。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"In the ASTM E119 tests of World Trade Center floor trusses that NIST commissioned from UL, the 35 ft unrestrained specimen achieved 2 hours while the restrained one achieved only 1.5 hours, contrary to expectation, a reminder that small-furnace results cannot simply be extrapolated to long spans and real restraint. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b093-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「外露環境、耐久與維護」與「改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Exposure, durability and maintenance\" and \"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b093-v13-33","title":"外露環境、耐久與維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Exposure, durability and maintenance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「外露鋼構厚塗環氧膨脹漆」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exterior thick-film epoxy intumescent” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"室內乾燥環境中的 SFRM 數十年幾乎不變，但外露或半外露構件要承受雨水、紫外線、溫濕循環與鹽分。薄塗型膨脹漆吸濕後可能失去膨脹能力，因此外露鋼構多採厚塗環氧型膨脹漆加耐候面漆；紐約時報大樓外露的角柱與橫梁即以約 80 或 120 mils（約 2 或 3 mm）的環氧膨脹漆一次噴塗，再滾平外觀。防火塗層同時擔任防蝕層，一旦面漆破損或膜下鏽蝕擴展，耐火與防蝕會一起失效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外露鋼構厚塗環氧膨脹漆」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"SFRM in dry interiors hardly changes for decades, but exposed or semi-exposed members face rain, ultraviolet light, thermal and humidity cycling and salt. Thin-film intumescents can lose their ability to expand after absorbing moisture, so exterior steel usually takes a thick-film epoxy intumescent with a weathering topcoat; the exposed corner columns and cross beams of the New York Times Building received epoxy intumescent sprayed in one coat at about 80 or 120 mils, about 2 or 3 mm, and back-rolled for appearance. The fire coating also acts as corrosion protection, so once the topcoat fails or rust creeps beneath the film, fire and corrosion protection fail together. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Exterior thick-film epoxy intumescent” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：面漆壽命 t = (初始厚度 − 最小厚度)/年損耗率。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Topcoat life t = (initial − minimum thickness)/annual loss.","failure":"常見誤解：「防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外露鋼構厚塗環氧膨脹漆」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Exterior thick-film epoxy intumescent”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-33-k1","title":"外露環境、耐久與維護","titleEn":"Exposure, durability and maintenance","text":"室內乾燥環境中的 SFRM 數十年幾乎不變，但外露或半外露構件要承受雨水、紫外線、溫濕循環與鹽分。薄塗型膨脹漆吸濕後可能失去膨脹能力，因此外露鋼構多採厚塗環氧型膨脹漆加耐候面漆；紐約時報大樓外露的角柱與橫梁即以約 80 或 120 mils（約 2 或 3 mm）的環氧膨脹漆一次噴塗，再滾平外觀。","textEn":"SFRM in dry interiors hardly changes for decades, but exposed or semi-exposed members face rain, ultraviolet light, thermal and humidity cycling and salt. Thin-film intumescents can lose their ability to expand after absorbing moisture, so exterior steel usually takes a thick-film epoxy intumescent with a weathering topcoat; the exposed corner columns and cross beams of the New York Times Building received epoxy intumescent sprayed in one coat at about 80 or 120 mils, about 2 or 3 mm, and back-rolled for appearance.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外露環境、耐久與維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exposure, durability and maintenance\" is correct?","options":["室內乾燥環境中的 SFRM 數十年幾乎不變，但外露或半外露構件要承受雨水、紫外線、溫濕循環與鹽分。","防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。","既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。"],"optionsEn":["SFRM in dry interiors hardly changes for decades, but exposed or semi-exposed members face rain, ultraviolet light, thermal and humidity cycling and salt.","Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.","If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"室內乾燥環境中的 SFRM 數十年幾乎不變，但外露或半外露構件要承受雨水、紫外線、溫濕循環與鹽分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"SFRM in dry interiors hardly changes for decades, but exposed or semi-exposed members face rain, ultraviolet light, thermal and humidity cycling and salt. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b093-v13-34","title":"外露環境、耐久與維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Exposure, durability and maintenance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外露鋼構厚塗環氧膨脹漆」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exterior thick-film epoxy intumescent” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：面漆壽命 t = (初始厚度 − 最小厚度)/年損耗率。面漆 60 μm、最低需保留 30 μm、外露面年損耗 5 μm：t = (60 − 30)/5 = 6 年；改用 80 μm 面漆則 t = 10 年。單位換算：80 mils × 25.4 μm/mil ≈ 2,030 μm，120 mils ≈ 3,050 μm。除單位換算外，數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Topcoat life t = (initial − minimum thickness)/annual loss. With a 60 μm topcoat, a 30 μm minimum and 5 μm/year loss on exposed faces: t = (60 − 30)/5 = 6 years; an 80 μm topcoat gives t = 10 years. Unit check: 80 mils × 25.4 μm/mil ≈ 2,030 μm and 120 mils ≈ 3,050 μm. Apart from the unit conversion, values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：正式施工前以實尺寸鋼構樣品做外觀與施工性試驗（紐約時報大樓曾在業主場址做過兩次鋼構樣品現場試驗），完工後建立分區基準照片與乾膜厚度圖；之後定期目視檢查粉化、龜裂、起泡與鏽水，抽量乾膜厚度與附著力，與基準比較決定局部修補或全面重塗面漆。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before production, apply the system to full-size steel mock-ups for appearance and workability (the New York Times Building ran two off-site field tests on steel mock-ups at the owner's facility), and after completion record zone-by-zone baseline photographs and DFT maps; then inspect periodically for chalking, cracking, blistering and rust staining, spot-check DFT and adhesion, and compare with the baseline to choose between local repair and full topcoat renewal.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"面漆壽命 t = (初始厚度 − 最小厚度)/年損耗率。面漆 60 μm、最低需保留 30 μm、外露面年損耗 5 μm：t = (60 − 30)/5 = 6 年；改用 80 μm 面漆則 t = 10 年。單位換算：80 mils × 25.4 μm/mil ≈ 2,030 μm，120 mils ≈ 3,050 μm。除單位換算外，數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Topcoat life t = (initial − minimum thickness)/annual loss. With a 60 μm topcoat, a 30 μm minimum and 5 μm/year loss on exposed faces: t = (60 − 30)/5 = 6 years; an 80 μm topcoat gives t = 10 years. Unit check: 80 mils × 25.4 μm/mil ≈ 2,030 μm and 120 mils ≈ 3,050 μm. Apart from the unit conversion, values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外露環境、耐久與維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exposure, durability and maintenance\", which statement holds?","options":["被覆厚度只依耐火時效決定，與鋼構件斷面大小無關。","面漆壽命 t = (初始厚度 − 最小厚度)/年損耗率。","膨脹型塗料只要總乾膜厚度足夠，底漆與面漆可以任意搭配。"],"optionsEn":["Protection thickness depends only on the required rating, not on the size of the steel section.","Topcoat life t = (initial − minimum thickness)/annual loss.","As long as the total dry film is thick enough, any primer and topcoat can be paired with an intumescent coating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面漆壽命 t = (初始厚度 − 最小厚度)/年損耗率。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Topcoat life t = (initial − minimum thickness)/annual loss. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b093-v13-35","title":"外露環境、耐久與維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exposure, durability and maintenance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外露鋼構厚塗環氧膨脹漆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exterior thick-film epoxy intumescent” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"正式施工前以實尺寸鋼構樣品做外觀與施工性試驗（紐約時報大樓曾在業主場址做過兩次鋼構樣品現場試驗），完工後建立分區基準照片與乾膜厚度圖；之後定期目視檢查粉化、龜裂、起泡與鏽水，抽量乾膜厚度與附著力，與基準比較決定局部修補或全面重塗面漆。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before production, apply the system to full-size steel mock-ups for appearance and workability (the New York Times Building ran two off-site field tests on steel mock-ups at the owner's facility), and after completion record zone-by-zone baseline photographs and DFT maps; then inspect periodically for chalking, cracking, blistering and rust staining, spot-check DFT and adhesion, and compare with the baseline to choose between local repair and full topcoat renewal. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：依環境分類選用經耐久評估的產品（如 ETAG 018-2 依室內、半外露與外露區分的類別），並在維護手冊列出檢查週期、允許的修補材料與修補後須量測的乾膜厚度；外露構件的任何塗層修補都要由原系統廠商確認相容性。","observationEn":"Site practice: Select products with a durability assessment matching the exposure, for example the internal, semi-exposed and exposed categories of ETAG 018-2, and list in the maintenance manual the inspection interval, permitted repair materials and the DFT to be measured after repair; every coating repair on exposed members needs compatibility confirmation from the original system manufacturer.","failure":"注意干擾：把室內型薄塗膨脹漆用於半外露的雨遮梁或停車場邊梁，數年後塗膜吸濕軟化、起泡，火災時膨脹不足；邊緣與螺栓頭等銳角處膜厚最薄，往往最先鏽蝕並從底部把塗層撐開。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using an interior thin-film intumescent on semi-exposed canopy or car-park edge beams lets the film absorb moisture, soften and blister within a few years, so it under-expands in a fire; sharp edges and bolt heads carry the thinnest film and are often the first to corrode and lift the coating from beneath. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"正式施工前以實尺寸鋼構樣品做外觀與施工性試驗（紐約時報大樓曾在業主場址做過兩次鋼構樣品現場試驗），完工後建立分區基準照片與乾膜厚度圖；之後定期目視檢查粉化、龜裂、起泡與鏽水，抽量乾膜厚度與附著力，與基準比較決定局部修補或全面重塗面漆。","textEn":"Before production, apply the system to full-size steel mock-ups for appearance and workability (the New York Times Building ran two off-site field tests on steel mock-ups at the owner's facility), and after completion record zone-by-zone baseline photographs and DFT maps; then inspect periodically for chalking, cracking, blistering and rust staining, spot-check DFT and adhesion, and compare with the baseline to choose between local repair and full topcoat renewal.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"依環境分類選用經耐久評估的產品（如 ETAG 018-2 依室內、半外露與外露區分的類別），並在維護手冊列出檢查週期、允許的修補材料與修補後須量測的乾膜厚度；外露構件的任何塗層修補都要由原系統廠商確認相容性。","textEn":"Select products with a durability assessment matching the exposure, for example the internal, semi-exposed and exposed categories of ETAG 018-2, and list in the maintenance manual the inspection interval, permitted repair materials and the DFT to be measured after repair; every coating repair on exposed members needs compatibility confirmation from the original system manufacturer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外露環境、耐久與維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exposure, durability and maintenance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","被覆驗收合格之後，後續工班的作業不會影響耐火性能。","正式施工前以實尺寸鋼構樣品做外觀與施工性試驗（紐約時報大樓曾在業主場址做過兩次鋼構樣品現場試驗），完工後建立分區基準照片與乾膜厚度圖。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once fireproofing passes acceptance, later trades cannot affect its fire performance.","Before production, apply the system to full-size steel mock-ups for appearance and workability (the New York Times Building ran two off-site field tests on steel mock-ups at the owner's facility), and after completion record zone-by-zone baseline photographs and DFT maps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"正式施工前以實尺寸鋼構樣品做外觀與施工性試驗（紐約時報大樓曾在業主場址做過兩次鋼構樣品現場試驗），完工後建立分區基準照片與乾膜厚度圖；之後定期目視檢查粉化、龜裂、起泡與鏽水，抽量乾膜厚度與附著力，與基準比較決定局部修補或全面重塗面漆。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before production, apply the system to full-size steel mock-ups for appearance and workability (the New York Times Building ran two off-site field tests on steel mock-ups at the owner's facility), and after completion record zone-by-zone baseline photographs and DFT maps; then inspect periodically for chalking, cracking, blistering and rust staining, spot-check DFT and adhesion, and compare with the baseline to choose between local repair and full topcoat renewal. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b093-v13-36","title":"外露環境、耐久與維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exposure, durability and maintenance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外露鋼構厚塗環氧膨脹漆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exterior thick-film epoxy intumescent” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把室內型薄塗膨脹漆用於半外露的雨遮梁或停車場邊梁，數年後塗膜吸濕軟化、起泡，火災時膨脹不足；邊緣與螺栓頭等銳角處膜厚最薄，往往最先鏽蝕並從底部把塗層撐開。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using an interior thin-film intumescent on semi-exposed canopy or car-park edge beams lets the film absorb moisture, soften and blister within a few years, so it under-expands in a fire; sharp edges and bolt heads carry the thinnest film and are often the first to corrode and lift the coating from beneath. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：防火塗層同時擔任防蝕層，一旦面漆破損或膜下鏽蝕擴展，耐火與防蝕會一起失效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The fire coating also acts as corrosion protection, so once the topcoat fails or rust creeps beneath the film, fire and corrosion protection fail together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「防火塗料只在火災時發揮作用，平時不需要檢查與維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fire-protective coatings only matter during a fire, so they need no routine inspection or maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把室內型薄塗膨脹漆用於半外露的雨遮梁或停車場邊梁，數年後塗膜吸濕軟化、起泡，火災時膨脹不足；邊緣與螺栓頭等銳角處膜厚最薄，往往最先鏽蝕並從底部把塗層撐開。","textEn":"Using an interior thin-film intumescent on semi-exposed canopy or car-park edge beams lets the film absorb moisture, soften and blister within a few years, so it under-expands in a fire; sharp edges and bolt heads carry the thinnest film and are often the first to corrode and lift the coating from beneath.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外露環境、耐久與維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exposure, durability and maintenance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把室內型薄塗膨脹漆用於半外露的雨遮梁或停車場邊梁，數年後塗膜吸濕軟化、起泡，火災時膨脹不足；邊緣與螺栓頭等銳角處膜厚最薄，往往最先鏽蝕並從底部把塗層撐開。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。"],"optionsEn":["Using an interior thin-film intumescent on semi-exposed canopy or car-park edge beams lets the film absorb moisture, soften and blister within a few years, so it under-expands in a fire.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把室內型薄塗膨脹漆用於半外露的雨遮梁或停車場邊梁，數年後塗膜吸濕軟化、起泡，火災時膨脹不足；邊緣與螺栓頭等銳角處膜厚最薄，往往最先鏽蝕並從底部把塗層撐開。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using an interior thin-film intumescent on semi-exposed canopy or car-park edge beams lets the film absorb moisture, soften and blister within a few years, so it under-expands in a fire; sharp edges and bolt heads carry the thinnest film and are often the first to corrode and lift the coating from beneath. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b093-v13-37","title":"改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「既有建築被覆升級」如何影響鋼構耐火被覆施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Retrofit upgrade of fireproofing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Structural-steel fireproofing application”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"既有鋼構建築常因法規更新、樓高分類或用途變更而需提高耐火時效，改修期間建築多半仍在使用，部分樓層已完成、部分尚未施作，防火區劃與被覆同時處於不完整狀態。馬德里溫莎大樓 2005 年火災時，外圍鋼柱的補強被覆只完成到第 17 層以下，未保護的上部外圍鋼柱在火中失效，上方樓層局部崩塌；世界貿易中心在 1990 年代把樓板桁架被覆由 1/2 in 提高到 1.5 in，也只完成部分樓層。改修計畫必須同時管控過渡期風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「既有建築被覆升級」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Existing steel buildings often need higher fire ratings after code updates, a change of height class or a change of use, and they usually stay occupied during the work, so some floors are finished and others not, with compartmentation and protection both incomplete. When the Windsor Building in Madrid burned in 2005, retrofit protection to the perimeter steel columns had been completed only below the 17th floor; the unprotected upper perimeter columns failed and upper storeys partly collapsed. The World Trade Center raised floor-truss protection from 1/2 in to 1.5 in in the 1990s, but only on some floors. A retrofit plan must manage the risk of the transition period. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Retrofit upgrade of fireproofing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：柱的厚度關係常寫成 R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Column thickness relations are often written R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h.","failure":"常見誤解：「既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「既有建築被覆升級」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Retrofit upgrade of fireproofing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-37-k1","title":"改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接","titleEn":"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover","text":"既有鋼構建築常因法規更新、樓高分類或用途變更而需提高耐火時效，改修期間建築多半仍在使用，部分樓層已完成、部分尚未施作，防火區劃與被覆同時處於不完整狀態。馬德里溫莎大樓 2005 年火災時，外圍鋼柱的補強被覆只完成到第 17 層以下，未保護的上部外圍鋼柱在火中失效，上方樓層局部崩塌；世界貿易中心在 1990 年代把樓板桁架被覆由 1/2 in 提高到 1.5 in，也只完成部分樓層。","textEn":"Existing steel buildings often need higher fire ratings after code updates, a change of height class or a change of use, and they usually stay occupied during the work, so some floors are finished and others not, with compartmentation and protection both incomplete. When the Windsor Building in Madrid burned in 2005, retrofit protection to the perimeter steel columns had been completed only below the 17th floor; the unprotected upper perimeter columns failed and upper storeys partly collapsed.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover\" is correct?","options":["既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。","既有鋼構建築常因法規更新、樓高分類或用途變更而需提高耐火時效，改修期間建築多半仍在使用，部分樓層已完成、部分尚未施作，防火區劃與被覆同時處於不完整狀態。","鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。"],"optionsEn":["If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating.","Existing steel buildings often need higher fire ratings after code updates, a change of height class or a change of use, and they usually stay occupied during the work, so some floors are finished and others not, with compartmentation and protection both incomplete.","Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame."],"answer":1,"explanation":"既有鋼構建築常因法規更新、樓高分類或用途變更而需提高耐火時效，改修期間建築多半仍在使用，部分樓層已完成、部分尚未施作，防火區劃與被覆同時處於不完整狀態。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Existing steel buildings often need higher fire ratings after code updates, a change of height class or a change of use, and they usually stay occupied during the work, so some floors are finished and others not, with compartmentation and protection both incomplete. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b093-v13-38","title":"改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「既有建築被覆升級」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Retrofit upgrade of fireproofing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：柱的厚度關係常寫成 R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h。取教學常數 C₁ = 1.05、C₂ = 0.61，W/D = 0.80：R/h = 1.05×0.80 + 0.61 = 1.45 h/in；2 小時需 h = 2/1.45 ≈ 1.38 in，升級為 3 小時需 3/1.45 ≈ 2.07 in，增加約 0.69 in（約 17.5 mm）。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Column thickness relations are often written R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h. With teaching constants C₁ = 1.05 and C₂ = 0.61 and W/D = 0.80: R/h = 1.05×0.80 + 0.61 = 1.45 h/in; 2 hours needs h = 2/1.45 ≈ 1.38 in, and an upgrade to 3 hours needs 3/1.45 ≈ 2.07 in, an increase of about 0.69 in (about 17.5 mm). Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：改修前以破壞性取樣確認既有被覆的產品、厚度、密度與黏結，判定可否直接加噴或必須全部清除；改修後依新建標準抽驗，並更新每層的被覆狀態圖，標示已完成、施工中與未施作區域，供消防單位與管理者掌握。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before retrofit, take destructive samples to establish the existing product, thickness, density and bond, and decide whether to overspray or strip completely; after retrofit sample to new-construction standards and update each floor's fireproofing status plan, marking completed, in-progress and untouched zones for the fire service and building management.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"柱的厚度關係常寫成 R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h。取教學常數 C₁ = 1.05、C₂ = 0.61，W/D = 0.80：R/h = 1.05×0.80 + 0.61 = 1.45 h/in；2 小時需 h = 2/1.45 ≈ 1.38 in，升級為 3 小時需 3/1.45 ≈ 2.07 in，增加約 0.69 in（約 17.5 mm）。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Column thickness relations are often written R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h. With teaching constants C₁ = 1.05 and C₂ = 0.61 and W/D = 0.80: R/h = 1.05×0.80 + 0.61 = 1.45 h/in; 2 hours needs h = 2/1.45 ≈ 1.38 in, and an upgrade to 3 hours needs 3/1.45 ≈ 2.07 in, an increase of about 0.69 in (about 17.5 mm). Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["噴覆材料越輕越隔熱，因此任何場所都應選用最低密度的產品。","只要噴得夠厚，鋼材表面的油汙或浮鏽不會影響被覆效果。","柱的厚度關係常寫成 R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h。"],"optionsEn":["Lighter fireproofing always insulates better, so the lowest-density product suits every location.","If it is sprayed thick enough, oil or loose rust on the steel does not affect the protection.","Column thickness relations are often written R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h."],"answer":2,"explanation":"柱的厚度關係常寫成 R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Column thickness relations are often written R = (C₁·W/D + C₂)·h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b093-v13-39","title":"改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「既有建築被覆升級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Retrofit upgrade of fireproofing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"改修前以破壞性取樣確認既有被覆的產品、厚度、密度與黏結，判定可否直接加噴或必須全部清除；改修後依新建標準抽驗，並更新每層的被覆狀態圖，標示已完成、施工中與未施作區域，供消防單位與管理者掌握。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before retrofit, take destructive samples to establish the existing product, thickness, density and bond, and decide whether to overspray or strip completely; after retrofit sample to new-construction standards and update each floor's fireproofing status plan, marking completed, in-progress and untouched zones for the fire service and building management. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：竣工交接應包含逐構件厚度表、登錄設計編號、檢驗報告、補修紀錄與產品資料，並在 BIM 或樓層圖標示被覆類型；任何改裝、用途變更或新增吊掛荷重前，須由結構與防火設計者評估，改修計畫的分區與臨時措施須經主管建築機關核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include the member-by-member thickness schedule, listing numbers, inspection reports, repair logs and product data, with protection types marked in BIM or floor plans; before any alteration, change of use or added suspended load, the structural and fire designers must assess the impact, and the building authority must approve the retrofit plan's phasing and temporary measures.","failure":"注意干擾：改修期間拆除層間防火阻隔與天花板卻未設臨時防火措施，火災會跨樓層蔓延並同時加熱多層未保護鋼材，溫莎大樓的報導即指出施工中層間防火阻隔曾被移除；新材料直接噴在老化或含石綿的舊被覆上，黏結失效時兩層會一起剝落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Removing floor-edge fire stops and ceilings during retrofit without temporary protection lets fire spread across storeys and heat several levels of unprotected steel at once, and reports on the Windsor Building note that fire stops between floors had been removed during the works; spraying new material straight over aged or asbestos-containing old protection can fail in bond and peel both layers off together. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"改修前以破壞性取樣確認既有被覆的產品、厚度、密度與黏結，判定可否直接加噴或必須全部清除；改修後依新建標準抽驗，並更新每層的被覆狀態圖，標示已完成、施工中與未施作區域，供消防單位與管理者掌握。","textEn":"Before retrofit, take destructive samples to establish the existing product, thickness, density and bond, and decide whether to overspray or strip completely; after retrofit sample to new-construction standards and update each floor's fireproofing status plan, marking completed, in-progress and untouched zones for the fire service and building management.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"竣工交接應包含逐構件厚度表、登錄設計編號、檢驗報告、補修紀錄與產品資料，並在 BIM 或樓層圖標示被覆類型；任何改裝、用途變更或新增吊掛荷重前，須由結構與防火設計者評估，改修計畫的分區與臨時措施須經主管建築機關核准。","textEn":"Handover should include the member-by-member thickness schedule, listing numbers, inspection reports, repair logs and product data, with protection types marked in BIM or floor plans; before any alteration, change of use or added suspended load, the structural and fire designers must assess the impact, and the building authority must approve the retrofit plan's phasing and temporary measures.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover\"?","options":["改修前以破壞性取樣確認既有被覆的產品、厚度、密度與黏結，判定可否直接加噴或必須全部清除。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","平均厚度達到設計值，就代表每一處都有足夠的保護。"],"optionsEn":["Before retrofit, take destructive samples to establish the existing product, thickness, density and bond, and decide whether to overspray or strip completely.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If the average thickness meets the design value, every location is adequately protected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"改修前以破壞性取樣確認既有被覆的產品、厚度、密度與黏結，判定可否直接加噴或必須全部清除；改修後依新建標準抽驗，並更新每層的被覆狀態圖，標示已完成、施工中與未施作區域，供消防單位與管理者掌握。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before retrofit, take destructive samples to establish the existing product, thickness, density and bond, and decide whether to overspray or strip completely; after retrofit sample to new-construction standards and update each floor's fireproofing status plan, marking completed, in-progress and untouched zones for the fire service and building management. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b093-v13-40","title":"改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"prerequisiteIds":["b093-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「既有建築被覆升級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Retrofit upgrade of fireproofing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"改修期間拆除層間防火阻隔與天花板卻未設臨時防火措施，火災會跨樓層蔓延並同時加熱多層未保護鋼材，溫莎大樓的報導即指出施工中層間防火阻隔曾被移除；新材料直接噴在老化或含石綿的舊被覆上，黏結失效時兩層會一起剝落。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Removing floor-edge fire stops and ceilings during retrofit without temporary protection lets fire spread across storeys and heat several levels of unprotected steel at once, and reports on the Windsor Building note that fire stops between floors had been removed during the works; spraying new material straight over aged or asbestos-containing old protection can fail in bond and peel both layers off together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：改修計畫必須同時管控過渡期風險。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A retrofit plan must manage the risk of the transition period.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「既有被覆只要外觀完整，就能直接加噴新材料達到更高的耐火時效。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If existing fireproofing looks intact, new material can simply be sprayed over it to reach a higher rating.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b093-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"改修期間拆除層間防火阻隔與天花板卻未設臨時防火措施，火災會跨樓層蔓延並同時加熱多層未保護鋼材，溫莎大樓的報導即指出施工中層間防火阻隔曾被移除；新材料直接噴在老化或含石綿的舊被覆上，黏結失效時兩層會一起剝落。","textEn":"Removing floor-edge fire stops and ceilings during retrofit without temporary protection lets fire spread across storeys and heat several levels of unprotected steel at once, and reports on the Windsor Building note that fire stops between floors had been removed during the works; spraying new material straight over aged or asbestos-containing old protection can fail in bond and peel both layers off together.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]},{"id":"b093-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改修升級、用途變更與竣工交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Retrofit upgrades, change of use and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","改修期間拆除層間防火阻隔與天花板卻未設臨時防火措施，火災會跨樓層蔓延並同時加熱多層未保護鋼材，溫莎大樓的報導即指出施工中層間防火阻隔曾被移除。","鋼材要到熔點（約 1,500°C）才會失去承載力，所以一般火災不足以讓鋼構倒塌。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Removing floor-edge fire stops and ceilings during retrofit without temporary protection lets fire spread across storeys and heat several levels of unprotected steel at once, and reports on the Windsor Building note that fire stops between floors had been removed during the works.","Steel only loses capacity near its melting point of about 1,500°C, so an ordinary fire cannot bring down a steel frame."],"answer":1,"explanation":"改修期間拆除層間防火阻隔與天花板卻未設臨時防火措施，火災會跨樓層蔓延並同時加熱多層未保護鋼材，溫莎大樓的報導即指出施工中層間防火阻隔曾被移除；新材料直接噴在老化或含石綿的舊被覆上，黏結失效時兩層會一起剝落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Removing floor-edge fire stops and ceilings during retrofit without temporary protection lets fire spread across storeys and heat several levels of unprotected steel at once, and reports on the Windsor Building note that fire stops between floors had been removed during the works; spraying new material straight over aged or asbestos-containing old protection can fail in bond and peel both layers off together. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-nist-icc-code-changes-2008","v13s-nist-wtc-ul-floor-tests","v13s-aisc-msc-fire-thickness","v13s-sci-new-york-times-building","v13s-nsc-lessons-from-madrid"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
